window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v3-index"]=[{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner narration","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"ch 1  cold open in her pov  the icarus gamble the volume opens inside chabashira s first person with no setting and no interlocutor   a soliloquy that retells the myth of daedalus and icarus and then states why she provoked a certain young boy  the myth  her summary  daedalus  confined in a tower by king minos alongside his son icarus  fashions wings of bird feathers  thread and wax  the warning  if you fly too high  the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together  be careful  icarus forgets it  the wax melts  and he falls into the sea and dies   for some reason  i thought of icarus  wings when standing before a certain young boy   considering what these past few months had brought  i could say that i made the comparison simply because he resembled icarus   but i immediately came to realize that the two boys were fundamentally different from one another  this boy possessed neither the bravery nor the arrogance of icarus   i had been pushed into a corner  i had no choice but to do it   the die cannot be returned once cast  the gamble had already begun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\">Ch.1: cold open in her POV, the Icarus gamble<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.10–12<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The volume opens inside Chabashira&#x27;s first person with no setting and no interlocutor — a soliloquy that retells the myth of Daedalus and Icarus and then states why she provoked a certain young boy.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The myth, her summary: Daedalus, confined in a tower by King Minos alongside his son Icarus, fashions wings of bird feathers, thread and wax; the warning “If you fly too high, the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together.…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;For some reason, I thought of Icarus’ wings when standing before a certain young boy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Considering what these past few months had brought, I could say that I made the comparison simply because he resembled Icarus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> The myth, her summary: Daedalus, confined in a tower by King Minos alongside his son Icarus, fashions wings of bird feathers, thread and wax; the warning “If you fly too high, the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together. Be careful.”; Icarus forgets it, the wax melts, and he falls into the sea and dies.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She frames her own predicament in classical myth — “Greek mythology deals abundantly with human frailty.” — treating her situation as a fable to be interpreted before it is confessed.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;But I immediately came to realize that the two boys were fundamentally different from one another. This boy possessed neither the bravery nor the arrogance of Icarus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I had been pushed into a corner. I had no choice but to do it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Cornered and out of means, she chose the provocation: incur the boy&#x27;s divine wrath and turn his quiet rage onto herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The die cannot be returned once cast. The gamble had already begun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Soliloquy register: measured, literary, fatalistic — she narrates her own decision as a fable already decided, with no hedging and no appeal for sympathy.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The boy is never named on these pages — only &quot;a certain young boy&quot; / &quot;this boy&quot;. Identity left open; not assigned from context.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cruise  the first name fever  and the boundary deck of the luxury liner on the way to the school s private island  first years of class d around him after midterms and finals  the chapter is his first person account   the endless summer sea  the infinite blue skies  the perfectly clear air  prices the trip honestly  on his own it  would probably have cost me about 100 000 yen  even in the off season  notes hirata s arrival as rescue   i was saved by the appearance of my hero  hirata man  on hirata and karuizawa cooling off   they seemed to get along well whenever i saw them talking  the chapter s thesis  stated before he understands it   i had yet to realize that this place was going to be the boundary between heaven and hell","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the first-name fever, and the boundary<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the luxury liner on the way to the school&#x27;s private island; first-years of Class D around him after midterms and finals.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter is his first-person account: &quot;The endless summer sea. The infinite blue skies. The perfectly clear air.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Prices the trip honestly: on his own it &quot;would probably have cost me about 100,000 yen, even in the off season.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes Hirata&#x27;s arrival as rescue: &quot;I was saved by the appearance of my hero, Hirata Man.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shoved by a Class A boy (&quot;Hey, you&#x27;re in the way. Move it, you defects.&quot;) and catches the railing; Sudou answers back, Class D is chased from the bow.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the hierarchy and swallows it: &quot;Although the situation was unfair, we didn&#x27;t need any unnecessary trouble, so it was best to ignore it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Hirata and Karuizawa cooling off: &quot;They seemed to get along well whenever I saw them talking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Feeds Sudou&#x27;s practice by inventing a wrong first name — &quot;Tomiko. Horikita Tomiko.&quot; — then corrects it to Suzune; keeps the joke to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Suspects Horikita&#x27;s hiding (&quot;a slight difference—something felt out of place&quot;) but drops it: &quot;it would be silly to investigate further. Best just to drop it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s thesis, stated before he understands it: &quot;I had yet to realize that this place was going to be the boundary between heaven and hell.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou mashima-tomonari ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 0    2 4  the cruise loudmouth who turns out to be the useful one deck of the liner  he opens the chapter with both hands in the air   whoa  this is the beeeeeeesssssst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0 &amp; §2.4: the cruise loudmouth who turns out to be the useful one<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–17, p.67–70<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; he opens the chapter with both hands in the air.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#mashima-tomonari\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Whoa! This is the beeeeeeesssssst!”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Teased by Yamauchi about his low final score; Sudou howls it off — &quot;With my skills, there was nothing to worry about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Declares the trip the occasion to confess; secures first-name permission — “Of course it’s okay for you to call me that. Should I call you Kanjikun, then?” — and cries the answer out to heaven.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Substitutes for Ayanokōji as Sudou&#x27;s practice-Horikita and gets choke-held for the gyaru performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The complaint Mashima answers seriously — &quot;We can’t all sleep together in just two tents!&quot; — which Mashima treats as a student operating below the programme&#x27;s level.<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Drinks the river on demand when challenged — &quot;Ah! Whew, that’s ice cold. It feels great! It’s damn good!&quot; — and gets the girls&#x27; disgust instead of trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The camping background surfaces properly: family trips as a child; he can read a clean water source on sight; first-ever expressed regret — &quot;I guess the stuff I said was probably a little unreasonable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69–70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.7–2.8: the bonfire, the apology, and the river vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke shinohara-satsuki yamauchi-haruki karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  she is the girls  standard  and she bends for the class points deck of the liner  the group of girls  led by karuizawa  comes out of the cabin  and she points at the ocean with a radiant smile   this view is incredible  i m honestly super moved right now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2: she is the girls&#x27; standard, and she bends for the class points<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13, p.42, p.96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; the group of girls &quot;led by Karuizawa&quot; comes out of the cabin, and she points at the ocean with a radiant smile.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “This view is incredible! I’m honestly super moved right now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The chapter opens on the pair cooling off — &quot;lately she and Hirata haven’t been very flirty with each other&quot; — without a fight and without tension.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> The unexpected toilet answer: “Well, I suppose it’ll be tough, but I really want class points. I guess I’ll just grin and bear it.” — and the block moves: &quot;If Karuizawa said as much, then even the strong-willed Shinohara couldn’t oppose her openly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The endurance stance nobody predicted from her; Ayanokōji flags it as &quot;An unexpected response from Karuizawa, who seemed like she would’ve been first to complain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Head of the &quot;Empress Team&quot; in Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the girls&#x27; groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cruise  the class a shove  and the name practice deck of the liner  survives the joke about his expulsion scoring final   with my skills  there was nothing to worry about  didn t i tell you i d prove myself  and it d be easy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the Class A shove, and the name practice<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; survives the joke about his expulsion-scoring final.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “With my skills, there was nothing to worry about. Didn’t I tell you I’d prove myself, and it’d be easy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Answers a Class A shove with intimidation and is talked down by the situation, not by fear — &quot;A fistfight didn’t break out, evidence that he was perhaps growing up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Forces Ayanokōji into imaginary-Horikita practice so he can ask for her first name; the look &quot;really creeped me out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Puts Ike in a chokehold for the gyaru performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1–§2.5: the toilet, the leader card, and a first calm intervention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 2  2 0 2 8  the target switch  the matches  and bringing ibuki in deck of the liner  insults sudou about his near expulsion while sudou laughs it off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0–§2.8: the target-switch, the matches, and bringing Ibuki in<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–17, p.73–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; insults Sudou about his near-expulsion while Sudou laughs it off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Goes oddly quiet during Ike&#x27;s Kushida campaign; never raises the subject again.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Confides the plan in a whisper — &quot;I think…I’m gonna go for Sakura&quot; — framing her as the reachable backup after Kushida; asks Ayanokōji to leave him alone with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets refused and recovers instantly — &quot;Jeez, you’re stiff. Well, fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Burns three matches and gets only smoke; runs off to ask the teacher and comes back to Ike&#x27;s finished fire.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The one who won&#x27;t walk past the swollen-cheeked Class C girl; insists the three of them wait until she moves.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Explains her situation to the class when Satō notices the interloper.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Maps the girls&#x27; teams for the boys — &quot;the Empress Team, led by Karuizawa… Kushida-chan’s Friendship Team… Shinohara’s Arrogant Team. Then you have Horikita and Sakura, who are by themselves&quot; — and wants to eat with the last of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the shirtless accusation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  the first name permission  the leader nomination  and the shared meal deck of the liner  the extraordinary view  had stolen her breath away","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\">Ch.2: the first-name permission, the leader nomination, and the shared meal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.14–20, p.66–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; the extraordinary view &quot;had stolen her breath away.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Grants Ike first-name permission and offers &quot;Kanjikun&quot; in return — the exchange that sets Ike&#x27;s confession plan running.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present when Sudou fumbles Horikita&#x27;s first name as Tomiko; the correction to Suzune lands in front of the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Nominates Horikita as spot-leader in the circle — Hirata and Karuizawa &quot;stand out too much,&quot; but responsibility is the criterion: &quot;I think that Horikita-san meets that criteria.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokōji reads the nomination as the least-risk play: Horikita &quot;was so desperate to reach Class A. That was crucial.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Walks over with a meal seat and water from her own group&#x27;s ration — four people sharing three portions — while Ibuki protests &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;Kushida, who wished for everyone’s happiness, had charity to spare.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Raises her hand for river water once the vote is already tipping, which Ayanokōji suspects is influence rather than conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0 2 2  the leader tries to hold a class that won t hold still deck of the liner  he pulls ayanokoji into the group the moment he appears","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.16, p.30–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; he pulls Ayanokōji into the group the moment he appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Called over as rescue; Hirata himself is too busy — &quot;Miyake-kun looks like he&#x27;s having trouble&quot; — and leaves for the cabins.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Asked why he isn&#x27;t with her: “We just kind of take things at our own pace.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads the watch rule as safety kit, not control: &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Opened the rules huddle that Ike&#x27;s complaints fracture into factions.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Breaks his own neutrality on the toilet: &quot;I&#x27;ve thought it over, and I believe we should install one toilet first&quot; — then beats Yukimura&#x27;s objection with the arithmetic of thirty-plus students sharing one box.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s verdict on the method: &quot;It wasn’t just to provoke arguments; he was convinced that he’d get their approval eventually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 0  she comes down from the ship wrong deck of the liner at disembark call  class d waits in the heat   i was just reading a book in my room  for whom the bell tolls  you wouldn t know it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.22–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner at disembark call; Class D waits in the heat.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I was just reading a book in my room. For Whom the Bell Tolls. You wouldn’t know it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Even Horikita, normally so meticulous, was concerned about her appearance. Right now, though, her hair was disheveled.&quot; — and she rubs her arms as if cold.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her stated excuse for locking herself away doesn&#x27;t cover what Ayanokōji saw; the chapter leaves the gap open.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner","w":"horikita-suzune hoshinomiya-chie ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 1 2 2  the test is announced  and class d splits three ways beach landing  mashima sensei announces the deserted island special test from a white platform  names the test s real shape   essentially  it was a contest of restraint","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">Ch.2 §2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–46<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach landing; Mashima-sensei announces the deserted-island special test from a white platform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the test&#x27;s real shape: &quot;Essentially, it was a contest of restraint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Works the rules the way the chapter needs them read: the penalties page &quot;will determine whether you live or die&quot;; the watches are safety kit — &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> First to ask the question that sets the economy: &quot;is it possible to get by without using any points?&quot; — Chabashira answers that the school &quot;isn&#x27;t involved in the test process at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands apart from the toilet fight, watching Hirata get pulled apart: &quot;I stood a short distance away, watching the situation unfold.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sidles up to her read of the class; she admits she can&#x27;t see a solution and he agrees — &quot;I think the same. There&#x27;s too much we don&#x27;t know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Given the season-opening advice about confessing to a girl before the ocean; wishes she would leave his love life alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the first-name fever, and the boundary<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ike-kanji chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  2 1  she runs the rules that sink the summer beach landing  she takes class d s roll call in the same jersey as the students   keeping on like that would be shameful  ike  so stop talking    and the world widening follow up   there are workplaces where there aren t any chairs in the office  and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls  the world is wider and deeper than you even know   in other words  you are ill equipped to distinguish between what is reality and what isn t     in my opinion  you re all equally worthless","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–39<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach landing; she takes Class D&#x27;s roll call in the same jersey as the students.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Keeping on like that would be shameful, Ike, so stop talking.” — and the world-widening follow-up: “There are workplaces where there aren’t any chairs in the office, and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls. The world…”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “In other words, you are ill-equipped to distinguish between what is reality and what isn’t.” / “In my opinion, you’re all equally worthless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Keeping on like that would be shameful, Ike, so stop talking.” — and the world-widening follow-up: “There are workplaces where there aren’t any chairs in the office, and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls. The world is wider and deeper than you even know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Delivers the penalty list verbatim from the manual — thirty for health retirement, twenty for pollution, five per absent student at roll call, disqualification plus private-point forfeiture for inter-class violence.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Assembles the cardboard toilet in front of the class and demonstrates the polymer sheet — &quot;five uses with one vinyl bag.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Explains the spot system: eight-hour rights of exclusive possession, one provisional bonus point per occupation, fifty-point penalty for using another class&#x27;s spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Brushes off the eavesdropping complaint and the &quot;fate&quot; line; threatens a behavioural report.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Refuses the emergency-bear question on process grounds: &quot;the test has already begun. I cannot answer any questions that might possibly influence your results.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Confirms the school &quot;isn’t involved in the test process at all&quot; — survival is the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: cold open in her POV, the Icarus gamble<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.8: she announces the retirement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 1  the announcement that erases the vacation a prepared white platform on the beach  uniformed adults setting up a tent and computers behind him   well then  we shall commence the current academic year s first special test   this test will determine if you can live on a deserted island together as a group  designed based on real world corporate training  sets the theme that names the chapter   the theme of this special exam is  freedom  after all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: the announcement that erases the vacation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–29<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#mashima-tomonari\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A prepared white platform on the beach; uniformed adults setting up a tent and computers behind him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Well then. We shall commence the current academic year’s first special test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “This test will determine if you can live on a deserted island together as a group… designed based on real-world corporate training.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Sets the theme that names the chapter: &quot;The theme of this special exam is ‘freedom’, after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Introduced as Class A&#x27;s homeroom teacher, English, &quot;well-known for having a stubborn disposition,&quot; built like a wrestler but &quot;actually quite intelligent&quot; — and he opens grim: &quot;it’s unfortunate that one of you was unable to participate due to illness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Answers Ike&#x27;s disbelief without contempt for the complaint itself, only for its basis — &quot;you’ve lived a short, superficial life. There is an actual, prominent company that holds training sessions on uninhabited islands.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Concedes the process complaint where he didn&#x27;t concede the disbelief: &quot;I suppose that you’re not wrong about that. I can understand why you would be discontented.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Hands out the three-hundred-point budget and the manual; frames the week as playable.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the stakes — remaining points convert to class points after vacation — and the Class A illness penalty: thirty points, leaving A at 270.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p32-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 1  the toilet war rules huddle on the beach  the cardboard toilet demonstration lands on the girls   don t tell me we have to use that    raised  in horrified surprise  at the assembled box","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: the toilet war<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.32–35, p.41–42<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Rules huddle on the beach; the cardboard toilet demonstration lands on the girls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yukimura-teruhiko\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Don’t tell me we have to use that?!” — raised &quot;in horrified surprise&quot; at the assembled box.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The argument that runs the section: &quot;Don’t screw around! It probably doesn’t matter to you boys.&quot; / &quot;It’s true though, isn’t it? You do seem to be really perverted.&quot; / &quot;A gentleman? Get real. You’re by far the top contender for biggest pervert.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Begs the girls&#x27; representative to back the 20-point temporary toilet — &quot;Karuizawa-san, say something, will you?&quot; — and is outvoted by Karuizawa&#x27;s endurance line.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Keeps pleading with Hirata as the only decision-maker she trusts: &quot;Hirata-kun is going to consider all of our opinions and decide. Right, Hirata-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Gets the discrimination charge from him for framing it as a girls-only need: &quot;Isn’t that simply a form of discrimination?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–§2.8: the river fight, the apology, and the vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 1  she asks the questions that price the test class d s first rules huddle on the beach after mashima s announcement   in the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points  what would happen    the question that establishes the floor at zero   i m the same as the others  i ve never lived in such an environment before  so i can t really make any predictions  what an unpleasant test    her first open admission that academics don t transfer here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.33–45<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D&#x27;s first rules huddle on the beach after Mashima&#x27;s announcement.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “In the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points, what would happen?” — the question that establishes the floor at zero.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m the same as the others. I’ve never lived in such an environment before, so I can’t really make any predictions… What an unpleasant test.” — her first open admission that academics don&#x27;t transfer here.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Stands beside Ayanokōji watching Hirata fail to decide: &quot;Class D has no leadership, which worries me. Besides, Hirata’s a pushover. He can’t even make one decision, can he?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks him to take her side on endurance; he agrees; Classes A and B are already moving into the forest while C and D still can&#x27;t start.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 1 2 5  the toilet  the leader card  and a first calm intervention","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.1–§2.5: the toilet, the leader card, and a first calm intervention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.33, p.66–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Opens the cardboard-toilet crisis by needing it before the explanation is finished.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Steps forward to take the leader role in her place — &quot;You don’t want to do it though, right? Don’t make her do it. I can do it in her place.&quot; — and the offer is what triggers her acceptance.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Chides her in an unusually calm tone — &quot;I know I’ve caused trouble for the class. That’s what I’m saying.&quot; — and offers the boiling compromise nobody expected from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Self-aware about his own record: &quot;If you keep antagonizing people with trivial crap, eventually it’s gonna come back to bite you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Refuses the branch run flatly and goes swimming instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the Class A shove, and the name practice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation that fails<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v3-p36-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 2  2 1  the corridor ambush beach side  during class d s rules huddle  she tackles chabashira from behind   what  i can t be friendly  i honestly wanted to see what you d do     whenever i touch your hair  sae chan  it s always so smooth   you need to be more carefree","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v3-p36-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v3-p36-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the corridor ambush<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.36–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach-side, during Class D&#x27;s rules huddle; she tackles Chabashira from behind.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “What, I can’t be friendly? I honestly wanted to see what you’d do.” / “Whenever I touch your hair, Sae-chan, it’s always so smooth!”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “You need to be more carefree!”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Gets the eavesdropping rebuke and the &quot;fate&quot; double-meaning ignored; leaves with a sad look when threatened with a behavioural report.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Spots him and opens the summer-love advice — &quot;Summer is the season of love. If you want to confess your feelings to a girl you like, perhaps it’d be more effective while standing before the beautiful ocean?&quot; — to his visible embarrassment.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v3-p42-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ike-kanji kouenji-rokusuke yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  the no points hardliner  and the day he folds joins the toilet fight uninvited  sliding his glasses up   it s not as though i don t understand the girls  desire to have a temporary toilet  however  i m not convinced that we ought to arbitrarily spend our points  i d like to at least make a decision after collecting a majority vote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v3-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the no-points hardliner, and the day he folds<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.42–43, p.50–51, p.90, p.98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yukimura-teruhiko\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Joins the toilet fight uninvited, sliding his glasses up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “It’s not as though I don’t understand the girls’ desire to have a temporary toilet. However, I’m not convinced that we ought to arbitrarily spend our points… I’d like to at least make a decision after collecting a majority vote.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The line the chapter keeps against him: “Even money can move based purely on instinct. I hate that women argue so emotionally.” — and Shinohara&#x27;s &quot;Huh?&quot; is the only response printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Loses the toilet vote to Hirata&#x27;s arithmetic — &quot;Fine. In that case, let’s install one toilet.&quot; — described as beaten: &quot;Yukimura, who couldn’t bear being stared at in silence, broke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Folds again when Ike sides with Hirata&#x27;s 120-point plan: &quot;Yukimura still appeared reluctant, but seeing Ike join with Hirata made him fold.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The outburst at the retirement — &quot;Kouenji, you jerk! What the hell…were you thinking?!&quot; — &quot;The normally silent Yukimura shouted and kicked the ground.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 2 2 3  he volunteers  and horikita s isolation is priced walking from beach toward the forest with the tent party  horikita trails the group alone  his standing theory of her  filed as interpretation not fact   horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother  she wasn t aiming for class a for her own sake  but rather  sought her older brother s approval","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">Ch.2 §2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach toward the forest with the tent party; Horikita trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His standing theory of her, filed as interpretation not fact: &quot;Horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother. She wasn&#x27;t aiming for Class A for her own sake, but rather, sought her older brother&#x27;s…<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her depression out loud — &quot;I can&#x27;t be alone&quot; — and his answer that this test is the one her academics can&#x27;t win; he watches her realise Ike and Sudou moved faster than she could.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His standing theory of her, filed as interpretation not fact: &quot;Horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother. She wasn&#x27;t aiming for Class A for her own sake, but rather, sought her older brother&#x27;s approval.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She blocks the probe — &quot;It doesn&#x27;t feel good to have someone pry into your past&quot; — and he retreats cleanly.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Raises his hand for the search party for a stated system reason: &quot;without a role to fill in the class, you&#x27;ll get cut off.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Paired by leftovers&#x27; logic with Sakura and Kouenji; notes the pairing works — &quot;I&#x27;d be able to move without any difficulty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  she admits the isolation  and blocks the probe walking from beach to forest  she trails the group alone   to be honest  i m depressed  these kinds of things just aren t for me  life on an island seems primitive  and worst of all  i can t be alone   it doesn t feel good to have someone pry into your past    and names chabashira as the leak   chabashira sensei leaked the information  don t misunderstand me  all right  besides  we re still not friends  don t forget that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “To be honest, I’m depressed. These kinds of things just aren’t for me. Life on an island seems primitive, and worst of all, I can’t be alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It doesn’t feel good to have someone pry into your past” — and names Chabashira as the leak: “Chabashira-sensei leaked the information. Don’t misunderstand me. All right? Besides, we’re still not friends. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes the classroom verdict against her own tools: &quot;This test will likely fall outside of my academic abilities. I’d determined that Ike-kun and Sudou-kun would be hindrances, but they took the initiative to go out searching. I wasn’t able to do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ends the exchange on her own terms before he can go deeper.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi","q":"ch 2  the forest team  the blush  and the second volunteer shift walking from beach to forest  she is at the back  watching ayanokoji s back   and looks away when he turns","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\">Ch.2: the forest team, the blush, and the second volunteer shift<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.48, p.52–63, p.74–97<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she is at the back, watching Ayanokōji&#x27;s back — and looks away when he turns.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Leftover-paired with him and Kouenji; trips on roots and he pulls her up, brushing dirt from her hands — &quot;S-sorry.&quot; / &quot;You don’t need to apologize.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Flusters and hurries forward when he asks why she raised her hand: &quot;Th-that’s not what I mean! It’s just that since there isn’t anyone I can talk to, that’s why…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Lends her handkerchief for the trail marker without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Goes &quot;almost comatose&quot; when he holds her hand through the Class A hide — &quot;I thought I was going to die. My heart stopped…&quot; — and adjusts her glasses as she recovers.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Surprisingly harsh on him in the moment: &quot;Kouenji-kun has been acting pretty funny from the start, so it’s okay.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Scared off by a single sharp look — &quot;Were you looking at me just now?&quot; — and runs to put distance between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Second volunteer shift, the branch run, after Sudou and Yamauchi refuse; &quot;if I stay here, well…it’ll be…a little uncomfortable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks whether he should have taken Ike&#x27;s fire credit himself; his answer moves her — &quot;like she was moved by my words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Eats alone at the edge of the groups; the boys&#x27; attention lands on her body while the chapter keeps her out of the conversation entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the class: she and Horikita are the two girls &quot;who are by themselves.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: chasing him into the forest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 3    2 8  the forest walk  and the retirement that costs thirty points volunteer circle for the forest search  he raises a hand last   the sun certainly is refreshing  my body needs energy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.3 &amp; §2.8: the forest walk, and the retirement that costs thirty points<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.52–63, p.97–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volunteer circle for the forest search; he raises a hand last, &quot;The sun certainly is refreshing. My body needs energy.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yukimura-teruhiko\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Answers Ayanokōji&#x27;s worry about getting lost with the perfect-human disclaimer — &quot;I am a perfect human being. I would never foolishly lose my way in a forest. If any problem occurs, it would most likely be because you two lost sight of me. When that happens, you should give up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the island in one line: &quot;I wouldn’t call this a natural forest. The probability of getting lost during the day is extremely low. It’s precisely for that reason that I’m a little curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Poses the question the ordinary pair can&#x27;t answer — &quot;What do you see when you look around?&quot; — accepts &quot;Common folk are simple, after all,&quot; and walks on.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Skipped the return and went swimming; Ayanokōji notes he ran off &quot;suggesting that he was already familiar with the forest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Retires from the test on a claimed poor physical condition; the class eats a thirty-point penalty; Chabashira states the rule — &quot;Kouenji has retired, and he’s obligated to stay onboard the ship for one week for medical treatment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The normally silent Yukimura shouts and kicks the ground at the news; the class is furious and can do nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the forest team  and class a s leader in the open forest path with kouenji ahead and sakura behind  damp heat  unstable footing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.53–62<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Forest path with Kouenji ahead and Sakura behind; damp heat, unstable footing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Hides them both when a Class A boy leaves the cave; overhears Katsuragi name himself leader and the cave as a spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Talks to her because she is the only one left to talk to; she trips on roots and he pulls her up, brushing dirt from her hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Borrows Sakura&#x27;s handkerchief and ties it to a branch as a trail marker — the chapter&#x27;s first quiet competence beat.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Slows his own pace so Sakura won&#x27;t feel like the problem: &quot;That way, Sakura wouldn&#x27;t feel like the problem. She probably saw through my ploy, but I didn&#x27;t mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the fatal leak on the spot — &quot;They had clearly made their leader known to us&quot; — and takes the report on himself so Sakura, who has poor communication skills, doesn&#x27;t have to carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Holds her hand through the hiding without meaning to; she goes &quot;almost comatose&quot; and he checks on her twice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"totsuka-yahiko sakayanagi-arisu ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the class a leader who showed his card a reinforced cave on the mountainside  he comes out and stands watch at the entrance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Class A leader who showed his card<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.59–62<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A reinforced cave on the mountainside; he comes out and stands watch at the entrance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sakayanagi-arisu\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Lectures his partner on the school&#x27;s hints — the ship&#x27;s deliberate circle around the island, the path visible from the deck — &quot;Finding it was inevitable. Be mindful of what you say and do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s model of Class A thinking: &quot;Before the ship docked at the pier, it had already taken a trip around…the island as a detour for some reason. That was probably a deliberate move by the school to give the students some hints.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named as the rival his partner expects to silence by holding the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The contempt line that frames Class D: &quot;Class D is just an assortment of failures, right? They’re defective. Considering the point difference, it’s probably fine to ignore them, right?&quot; — overruled as enough chit-chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Identified by the watchers as Class A&#x27;s spot-leader holding the key card — a mistake Ayanokōji files as &quot;a fatal mistake&quot; for the seventh-day guess rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the second man in the cave inside and around the class a cave with katsuragi on day one   in a cave this size  we should have enough room for two tents  katsuragi san  we sure were lucky  we secured a spot really quickly    corrected on the spot  luck was inference   i didn t notice anything at all  and yet  katsuragi san  you managed to see the school s true intentions  because of that  you understood there was a cave here  just as we d expect from you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the second man in the cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.59–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Inside and around the Class A cave with Katsuragi on day one.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sakayanagi-arisu\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “In a cave this size, we should have enough room for two tents, Katsuragi-san. We sure were lucky. We secured a spot really quickly.” — corrected on the spot: luck was inference.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “I didn’t notice anything at all, and yet… Katsuragi-san, you managed to see the school’s true intentions. Because of that, you understood there was a cave here. Just as we’d expect from you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “If we leave it like this, Sakayanagi will have no choice but to be quiet!” — the only Sakayanagi naming in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Carries the Class D contempt his leader overrules: &quot;Considering the point difference, it’s probably fine to ignore them, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: holding the entrance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 5  the river camp  the leader vote  and horikita s favour back at the assembly point  ike s group reports a river with a possession device ten minutes away  prices her isolation as the test s real subject   an academically brilliant girl was less useful than a normal student in a situation like this  and  this week would test horikita suzune s limits  and show her at her worst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">Ch.2 §2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back at the assembly point; Ike&#x27;s group reports a river with a possession device ten minutes away.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Prices her isolation as the test&#x27;s real subject: &quot;An academically brilliant girl was less useful than a normal student in a situation like this.&quot; and &quot;This week would test Horikita Suzune&#x27;s limits, and show her at her worst.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Answer for both of them to her question about Kouenji — &quot;I can&#x27;t control that guy. You know that.&quot; — then deflects her glare when she asks what he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> In the leader vote, reads the room instead of speaking: Kushida&#x27;s nomination of Horikita is &quot;the least risky choice, since she was so desperate to reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Personally relieved Sudou wasn&#x27;t chosen: &quot;I was relieved that someone like Sudou or Ike wasn&#x27;t the leader.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She delegates the Ike problem to him — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it&quot; — and he takes the timing as his own: &quot;I&#x27;ll talk to him, but leave the timing to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 8  the river  the 120 point speech  and taking ibuki in receives ike s river report and moves the class toward a base camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Receives Ike&#x27;s river report and moves the class toward a base camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Praised the find — &quot;Amazing, Ike-kun!&quot; — then takes his name to Chabashira as leader-candidate filing errand-boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Files Horikita&#x27;s name and hands her the card; orchestrates the fake collective touch to hide the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Breaks up the Ike–Shinohara round two and buys time: &quot;Let’s try breaking apart for a bit. We still have some time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Asks Ayanokōji for branches, apologetically — &quot;I can’t force you to agree&quot; — because light is necessary whether or not points get spent.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s centrepiece speech: sets the realistic floor at 120 points left, walks the class through the meal maths (10-point sets, 12 meals, 120 points), then reframes endurance as upside — &quot;If we can find drinking water for the week, we’ll save fifty points or more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji&#x27;s read: &quot;Anyone else could have come up with this, but Hirata’s tone and presentation sold it. He’d performed flawlessly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Takes the injured Class C girl in: &quot;We can’t just leave someone in trouble. We all think so.&quot; — and turns the spy question on its head: &quot;If you really were a spy, you wouldn’t want to be chased out, would you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Leaves Sakura out of the Ibuki escort — Ayanokōji reads it as pretty-boy thoughtfulness.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Distributes the evening meal while Kushida feeds Ibuki from her own group&#x27;s portion.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 4  the leader s card  and the favour she can t do herself the circle that picks class d s spot leader   i understand  i accept    after sudou tries to take the role to spare her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The circle that picks Class D&#x27;s spot-leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I understand. I accept.” — after Sudou tries to take the role to spare her.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida nominates her as the responsible choice; she accepts without visible surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Becomes Class D&#x27;s designated leader; Hirata files her name with Chabashira and the card is handed over; the class touches the device together to hide who holds it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His defence of her wishes is the trigger that makes her take the role rather than dodge it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delegates the Ike problem — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it. Can I count on you?&quot; — then delivers the standard put-down: “I suppose it must be relaxing to be unreliable and underachieving. … Isn’t it, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s closing read of her: alone she is &quot;amazing…but only alone&quot;; the school &quot;had made her isolated life impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p67-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 8  the river fight  the apology  and the vote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4–§2.8: the river fight, the apology, and the vote<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.67–68, p.88, p.91<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The drinking-water round: &quot;Then you drink it, as an experiment.&quot; → his gulp → &quot;Okay, that’s a major turn off. No way, no way! … Gross!&quot; / &quot;No way! Ugh, I hate barbarians like you most of all, god!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Mocks Sudou&#x27;s cooperation line — &quot;Oh, don’t make me laugh. Cooperate? That’s funny coming from you, Sudou-kun.&quot; — and then tells him to stop with the thoughtful suggestions.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Accepts his apology and answers with her own: &quot;I think I got way too emotional. We won’t be able to keep any of our points if we don’t learn to adjust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The holdout who converts last: &quot;I don’t know if I can drink it, but…I’m up for the challenge.&quot; — after Ike offers Sudou&#x27;s boiling plan as the on-ramp.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Head of the &quot;Arrogant Team&quot; in Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the girls&#x27; groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the toilet war<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 5 2 6  branches  yamauchi s plan  and the bonfire evening at the river camp  hirata asks him to gather branches for a bonfire","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">Ch.2 §2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.72–77<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at the river camp; Hirata asks him to gather branches for a bonfire.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">After Sudou and Yamauchi refuse, Sakura volunteers and he lets her; Yamauchi then reverses and joins.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi confides the switch from Kushida to Sakura as a body-driven target plan; he refuses the ask — &quot;I&#x27;d like to go back and start the bonfire while it&#x27;s still early.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Declines on her behalf rather than leaving her alone with &quot;some guy who only wanted to get into her pants.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Diagnoses the failed fire when Yamauchi cannot — damp wood, branches too thick — and stays quiet so Ike can be the one to fix it.<span class=\"pg\">p.84–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Explains the quiet help to Sakura: &quot;building up Ike and displaying his usefulness will be more helpful to the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 5    2 8  she refuses the assistantship  and votes last","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.73–74, p.92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On becoming Hirata&#x27;s assistant: “Me, his assistant? Don’t joke around. I’d rather dance with a mongoose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Names her own usable condition — &quot;If there were a clear enemy and a goal, I might be of…use&quot; — and admits she still can&#x27;t decide how far the class should spend.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises her hand for river water last, with Ayanokōji, after the whole class has already committed.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 6 2 7  ibuki  and the decision not to leave her walking back with branches  a girl from another class sits against a tree with a red  swollen mark on her cheek","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">Ch.2 §2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–86<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking back with branches; a girl from another class sits against a tree with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Stops Yamauchi from walking past her; the three of them agree to wait rather than leave an injured girl in the jungle.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Answers her &quot;I&#x27;m from Class C. In other words, I&#x27;m your enemy&quot; with &quot;That wasn&#x27;t any reason not to help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Says the camp-location leak won&#x27;t be a problem when she names the risk — the chapter never says why he is sure.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Introduces himself properly and holds the space while Hirata works the crowd: &quot;Sorry. Can you wait a little longer? I&#x27;m going to talk to him about you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Watches Hirata take Ibuki in and wonders why he was the one left with her: &quot;I wondered if Hirata had left me with her because he trusted me, or at least trusted me more than Yamauchi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 6 2 8  the class c girl with the swollen cheek a path in the forest on the way back to camp  she sits against a large tree  not a class d student  with a red  swollen mark on her cheek","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\">Ch.2 §2.6–§2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A path in the forest on the way back to camp; she sits against a large tree, not a Class D student, with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Just a class dispute. Don’t worry about it&quot; — her answer when asked who did it; &quot;her voice was low and even, but it was clear she wasn’t feeling well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the barrier herself: “I’m from Class C. In other words, I’m your enemy. You understand that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Refuses the base-camp offer — &quot;There’s no way I could do something like that&quot; — then watches them refuse to leave: &quot;You guys are really stupid. You’re not acting logically. You aren’t thinking about your own class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Introductions after the standoff: “I’m…Ibuki” — and she won&#x27;t meet his eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Dirt under her nails and disturbed soil where she sat — the page shows the fight without naming who won it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The account, once Hirata&#x27;s offer sticks: &quot;I had a fight with a boy in my class. He hit me and chased me away. That’s all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> On his decency: “He’s seriously a good-natured guy, isn’t he?” — and the Class C verdict: &quot;Not at all… There isn’t really anyone in Class C like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Gets Kushida&#x27;s group ration — &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot; — and is told to eat first, talk later.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Told to wait while the class decides; the class agrees to shelter her once roll-call attrition makes it profitable, not only decent.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"shinohara-satsuki hirata-yousuke sakura-airi ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 7 2 8  the bonfire  the apology  and the river vote evening at camp  yamauchi s matches have failed for the last time","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\">Ch.2 §2.7–2.8: the bonfire, the apology, and the river vote<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.85–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at camp; Yamauchi&#x27;s matches have failed for the last time.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Takes over without being asked — dead leaves, thin twigs, then thicker branches — and the fire is up &quot;in the blink of an eye.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The bonfire doubles as a smoke signal: &quot;If you can see the smoke, you’ll be able to find the campsite even if you get lost.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Walks the apology himself before she can: &quot;I was pushy because I wanted to save points. I’m sorry.&quot; — and remembers the first awful family camping toilet to explain why he now gets the girls&#x27; side.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She answers in kind; Ayanokōji reads the pair as having &quot;made up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Runs the river-water vote as a free poll, not a whip; when Shinohara hesitates he offers Sudou&#x27;s boiling plan as the on-ramp; nearly half the boys raise hands, then the girls, then everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.91–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes the formal camp job — &quot;W-well, I guess if you ask, I gotta cooperate&quot; — the class&#x27;s only camping expertise on payroll.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Ogles Sakura&#x27;s body with Yamauchi blocking the view; the chapter keeps the leering and the competence in the same character without joining them.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0 &amp; §2.4: the cruise loudmouth who turns out to be the useful one<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the chips at his feet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke ibuki-mio kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 8  the points speech  the river vote  and kouenji s exit five o clock  kushida s group returns with fruit  the bonfire is up  and the class settles into its first night  on kouenji s retirement   maybe he didn t care about reaching class a  if it made his life easier  losing thirty points didn t matter at all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.87–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Five o&#x27;clock; Kushida&#x27;s group returns with fruit, the bonfire is up, and the class settles into its first night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On Kouenji&#x27;s retirement: &quot;Maybe he didn&#x27;t care about reaching Class A. If it made his life easier, losing thirty points didn&#x27;t matter at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Credits Ike, not himself, for the fire: &quot;You should be thanking Ike, not me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Tries to raise the Ibuki report during the excitement and gets no opening: &quot;I didn&#x27;t have any chance to butt in.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Keeps his word to her while the class votes on river water.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises his hand for the river last, with Horikita, after everyone else — the chapter frames it as compliance, not conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Backs the fishing-rod plan as the cheap test it is: &quot;the cost was so minimal that it couldn&#x27;t really hurt us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-satou-maya-y1v3-p93-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio satou-maya","q":"ch 2  2 8  she spots the interloper evening at the river camp  during the food discussion   by the way  that girl  ibuki san from class c  i ve seen her before    eyed ibuki with suspicion from across the camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-satou-maya-y1v3-p93-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.8: she spots the interloper<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#satou-maya\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at the river camp, during the food discussion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> “By the way… That girl, Ibuki-san from Class C? I’ve seen her before.” — eyed Ibuki with suspicion from across the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Her naming is what moves Ibuki from background problem to class agenda; Yamauchi then supplies the explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  2 8  she announces the retirement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">Ch.2 §2.8: she announces the retirement<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.97–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Reads the class the cost of Kouenji&#x27;s exit without inflection: &quot;Kouenji complained about being in poor physical condition and returned to the ship. Of course, that means that you’ve had thirty points deducted. Those are the rules, so there’s nothing to be done.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  the camera in the luggage  the morning watch  kanzaki s visit pre dawn heat in the class d tent  ayanokoji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage   i guess if i had to pick  school life s my priority  besides  i don t think it s possible to reach class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–104<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pre-dawn heat in the Class D tent; Ayanokōji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I guess if I had to pick, school life&#x27;s my priority. Besides, I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s possible to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The island morning: the mesh tent keeps the night breeze, the luggage is stacked outside to save space, and dawn comes on hot.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens Ibuki&#x27;s singularly colored bag and finds a digital camera with a rental sticker — “This item wasn&#x27;t appropriate for a deserted island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Checks the camera&#x27;s power source — “It had no data, and no sign that it&#x27;d been used.” — returns it to the bag, and reasons out why she would carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The camera explains the dull sound he heard when she dropped the bag against a tree the day before.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Shares the early watch with Hirata while the rest of the class sleeps on.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After everyone is asleep, cuts one of the manual&#x27;s five blank pages, replicates a simple island map, folds it into a small square and pockets it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads the heart-bedazzled gifts in Hirata&#x27;s pack as Karuizawa&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Meets Kanzaki at the river with Hirata and takes in the Class B campsite directions.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Weighs that Kanzaki, Ichinose and Horikita had worked together in the false accusation case — probably why he thinks they are still on good terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads the visit as reconnaissance — “You could estimate the number of points spent just by the number of toilets, showers, and tents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The second spot update was postponed so ownership expires right after eight o&#x27;clock, letting the roll-call crowds camouflage the renewal.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei kanzaki-ryuuji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  the morning watch and the point arithmetic awake before the class in the crowded tent  greets ayanokoji slipping out  his back aching without a mattress   if you include kouenji kun s penalty  we spent almost 100 points yesterday  i told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we d be left with 120 points  but now i m not even sure about that  i guess the anxiety woke me   i m only doing this because i like it  if my hard work makes everyone in class happy  then i m satisfied  but it s surprisingly difficult   i wonder if our strategy s wrong  even if we can t beat the other classes  i thought it d be good for us to unify on this test  that s the real reason i don t want them to discover our leader   thank you  coming from you  that honestly makes me really happy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–105<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Awake before the class in the crowded tent; greets Ayanokōji slipping out, his back aching without a mattress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “If you include Kouenji-kun&#x27;s penalty, we spent almost 100 points yesterday. I told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we&#x27;d be left with 120 points, but now I&#x27;m not even sure about that. I guess the anxiety woke me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I&#x27;m only doing this because I like it. If my hard work makes everyone in class happy, then I&#x27;m satisfied. But it&#x27;s surprisingly difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I wonder if our strategy&#x27;s wrong. Even if we can&#x27;t beat the other classes, I thought it&#x27;d be good for us to unify on this test. That&#x27;s the real reason I don&#x27;t want them to discover our leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Cannot answer the Class A question — “That&#x27;s hard to answer. Aiming for the upper classes means forcing everyone… I&#x27;m sorry, I need to think on it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Adjusts his position so Ayanokōji can read the manual comfortably — “small acts of consideration” noted from the other side.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Carries her heart-bedazzled gifts in his pack and confirms it — “Spot on. How&#x27;d you guess?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Greets Kanzaki by name and accepts the apology for the early visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Coming from you, that honestly makes me really happy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Plans the sleeping-arrangement poll at the river, then after roll call assigns roles to the reliable students — Class D&#x27;s point-saving start.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  the camera in her bag the luggage pile outside the tent before dawn  her singularly colored bag is easy to spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The luggage pile outside the tent before dawn; her singularly colored bag is easy to spot.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her rented digital camera — no data, no sign it was ever used — is found in the bag while she sleeps and put back untouched.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.6–§2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 3  the river meeting appears at the river with two class b boys in the early morning  surprised to meet class d up and out   first day s over  so i wondered how you were doing  i thought i d check on you  your location s great   did i surprise you  i m sorry  i m not here to cause trouble   there are large broken trees along the path from here to the beach  if you enter the forest to the southwest and walk a bit  you can find our campsite  you shouldn t get lost if you enter by those large trees  if you need something  go ahead and tell her you can come by","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1\">Ch.3: the river meeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.103<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears at the river with two Class B boys in the early morning, surprised to meet Class D up and out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “First day&#x27;s over, so I wondered how you were doing. I thought I&#x27;d check on you. Your location&#x27;s great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Did I surprise you? I&#x27;m sorry, I&#x27;m not here to cause trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “There are large broken trees along the path from here to the beach. If you enter the forest to the southwest and walk a bit, you can find our campsite. You shouldn&#x27;t get lost if you enter by those large trees. If you need…”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Apologizes to him directly; Hirata greets him by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gives Ayanokōji the Class B campsite location without hesitating.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are large broken trees along the path from here to the beach. If you enter the forest to the southwest and walk a bit, you can find our campsite. You shouldn&#x27;t get lost if you enter by those large trees. If you need something, go ahead and tell her you can come by.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The invitation names no one — the her is read across as Ichinose from the false-accusation case, an inference on Ayanokōji&#x27;s side.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: at his own camp while Class D visits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ike-kanji ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 1  class c comes to provoke morning roll call over  exploration begins  two class c boys stride into the campsite eating chips","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning roll call over, exploration begins; two Class C boys stride into the campsite eating chips.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Recognizes Komiya and Kondou and recalls their earlier fight with Sudō as acting on Ryūen&#x27;s orders rather than just looking for a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The campsite after roll call, the river base holding, Class D setting out to explore.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Stands with Ike when the chips are tossed at his feet; neither takes the bait until Hirata&#x27;s group returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Files Ibuki&#x27;s worst-case remark and decides telling Horikita “seemed like a good idea.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pulls the leader out of the tent — “You&#x27;ve got eyes on Ryuuen, and you&#x27;ve even been observing Ichinose. People will remember that you&#x27;re the student council president&#x27;s younger sister. No matter what you do, you&#x27;ll be a target.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 1  the visit to the campsite class c s boys stride into the campsite  a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide   do you know ryuuen   i don t think they were looking for me   i wonder if things are heading toward that worst case scenario i imagined","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class C&#x27;s boys stride into the campsite; a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Do you know Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I don&#x27;t think they were looking for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I wonder if things are heading toward that worst-case scenario I imagined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sounds irritated discussing him — “as if she were discussing a family enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Komiya and Kondou are his underlings; his name alone puts her behind the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"komiya-kyogo ike-kanji","q":"ch 3  3 1  the chips at his feet the provocation reaches him in the middle of the campsite   what the hell  you guys","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the chips at his feet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The provocation reaches him in the middle of the campsite.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#komiya-kyogo\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “What the hell, you guys?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The chips bag lands at his feet; he snaps at the two Class C boys for ten minutes until Hirata&#x27;s group returns and they leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> The visit is aimed at his temper — Komiya and Kondou keep snacking while they bait him.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.7–2.8: the bonfire, the apology, and the river vote<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p141-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the camp greeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji kondou-reo komiya-kyogo","q":"ch 3  3 1  the campsite visit strides into the class d campsite with kondo  chips and soda in hand  smug grins on   wow  you class d rejects are really living frugal  eh  i guess that s what i d expect from a class of defectives   we have a message from ryuuen san  if you want to enjoy your summer vacation to the fullest  come to the beach right now  don t hang back  if you re sick of living like idiots  then we re happy to share our luxuries","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the campsite visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#komiya-kyogo\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Strides into the Class D campsite with Kondō, chips and soda in hand, smug grins on.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kondou-reo\">Kondō Reo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “Wow, you Class D rejects are really living frugal, eh? I guess that&#x27;s what I&#x27;d expect from a class of defectives.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “We have a message from Ryuuen-san. If you want to enjoy your summer vacation to the fullest, come to the beach right now. Don&#x27;t hang back. If you&#x27;re sick of living like idiots, then we&#x27;re happy to share our luxuries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation voices the taunt and the whole visit to the pair without saying which of them speaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tosses a bag of potato chips near Ike&#x27;s feet and keeps snacking for ten minutes until Hirata&#x27;s group returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Bait him directly; he snaps and they ignore him.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kondō Reo<\/b> Enters with Kondō; their voices are never separated on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The pair who once fought Sudō, recalled as acting on Ryūen&#x27;s orders rather than looking for a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kondou-reo-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"komiya-kyogo kondou-reo","q":"ch 3  3 1  the campsite visit follows komiya into the class d campsite during the morning provocation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kondou-reo-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the campsite visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kondou-reo\">Kondō Reo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Komiya into the Class D campsite during the morning provocation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#komiya-kyogo\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> Partner in every line of the visit — the taunts, the chip toss, the message — the translation never separates their voices.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> One of the two who fought Sudō; Ayanokōji recalls them as “acting on orders from Ryuuen, rather than just looking for a fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 1  called out of the tent summoned from the girls  tent after the class c provocation  the cloth moves  and she steps out   the cheap provocation coming from class c  yes  i heard   i don t want to move too much  since i m the leader  if i stand out too much  we ll be in a bad spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.106–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned from the girls&#x27; tent after the Class C provocation; the cloth moves, and she steps out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “The cheap provocation coming from Class C? Yes, I heard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I don&#x27;t want to move too much. Since I&#x27;m the leader, if I stand out too much, we&#x27;ll be in a bad spot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes she cannot stay hidden — the president&#x27;s younger sister, seen watching Ryūen and Ichinose: “You&#x27;re right. I suppose I can&#x27;t say what&#x27;s correct. Fine. I&#x27;m rather concerned about the state of the other classes. Let&#x27;s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes his read that hiding will not change anything and sets out with him for the Class C beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 2  ryuen s beach  spent to zero the class c beach  temporary toilets and showers  a tarp  a barbecue  chairs  a parasol  jet skis on the shoreline   it s up to you  horikita   that s simple  he d just do what kouenji did","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach: temporary toilets and showers, a tarp, a barbecue, chairs, a parasol, jet skis on the shoreline.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It&#x27;s up to you, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That&#x27;s simple. He&#x27;d just do what Kouenji did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class C shore: cooking smoke, laughter, a hundred and fifty points or more already burned.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line names Horikita as the one addressed; the translation never tags the speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands through Ryūen pouring out his water and throwing the warm bottle back at Ishizaki without intervening.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Leaves with her after the first-name call and the crotch-grab provocation, stopping once on the way back to look over the Class C camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the zero-points strategy: nothing left to penalize, and even guesses of every rival leader&#x27;s identity could gain only “a maximum of 150 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The plan at zero points is retirement — “His physical condition was poor and he was mentally unstable. In that case, it&#x27;s better to just retire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange never tags its speakers until Horikita&#x27;s final line; these lines are recorded here as the responses to her questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 2  the confrontation on the beach the class c beach spectacle  she cannot believe what she is looking at   no way  all this stuff  is it even possible   if the person on top is incompetent  those below him will suffer  this is pitiful   we re trying to warn you  you re an idiot   there is one more piece of business  you know ibuki  of course   you used up all your points on the first day  didn t you   see you later  suzune   i don t know where exactly you found that out  but do not call me by my first name so casually","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach spectacle; she cannot believe what she is looking at.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “No way… All this stuff… Is it even possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “If the person on top is incompetent, those below him will suffer. This is pitiful,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We&#x27;re trying to warn you. You&#x27;re an idiot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Walks up to his chair with Ayanokōji and holds the confrontation to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the line untagged; his reply is thrown back at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Asks who hit Ibuki roundabout — “Her face is swollen. Who did that to her?” — and gets the admission of a light punishment.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is one more piece of business. You know Ibuki, of course?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You…used up all your points on the first day, didn&#x27;t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know where exactly you found that out, but do not call me by my first name so casually.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Also untagged; she is the one addressed by the first-name call.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 3  3 2  the beach at zero holds court on the class c beach in swimwear   tanned  laid back in his chair  flashing white teeth   just as you see  we re enjoying our summer vacation   hmm  well  i didn t make a precise calculation   class d  the lowest of all  has to put up with starvation  heat  and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points  it makes me laugh   i said to bring me cold water  this water s warm   cooperation  don t make me laugh  people betray each other with ease  people lie  relationships built on trust just aren t viable  you can only trust yourself   i absolutely loathe hard work  patience  saving  you must be joking   ah  she ran out of here rather suddenly  she went looking for help from another class in the end  pathetic girl   another boy defied me as well  so i had him driven out  i heard he didn t die  so he s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive   ha ha ha  what should i do  i wonder  well  i suppose that plain  ordinary people can only engage in plain  ordinary thinking   see you later  suzune   well  i rather like forceful women  i ll make you submit to me eventually  when that time comes  it will be the ultimate pleasure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the beach at zero<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.109–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds court on the Class C beach in swimwear — tanned, laid back in his chair, flashing white teeth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Just as you see. We&#x27;re enjoying our summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Hmm. Well, I didn&#x27;t make a precise calculation,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Class D, the lowest of all, has to put up with starvation, heat, and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points. It makes me laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pours his remaining water on the sand “almost in provocation” while Ishizaki fetches another bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said to bring me cold water. This water&#x27;s warm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Ryuuen&#x27;s pupils were just like those of a snake.” — the returned bottle comes back in Ishizaki&#x27;s face.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cooperation? Don&#x27;t make me laugh. People betray each other with ease. People lie. Relationships built on trust just aren&#x27;t viable. You can only trust yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I absolutely loathe hard work. Patience? Saving? You must be joking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. She ran out of here rather suddenly. She went looking for help from another class in the end? Pathetic girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Admits her light punishment was a slap — he gestures it — and offers forgiveness only on his terms: “If she grovels on the ground, I&#x27;ll forgive her. I&#x27;ve a tolerant heart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another boy defied me as well, so I had him driven out. I heard he didn&#x27;t die, so he&#x27;s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Spent the entire three-hundred-point budget on day one — “Yes, as you said. I used all of our points.” — so there is nothing left to penalize.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha. What should I do, I wonder? Well, I suppose that plain, ordinary people can only engage in plain, ordinary thinking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her by her first name against her refusal, and answers her disgust while touching himself under the bathing suit.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I rather like forceful women. I&#x27;ll make you submit to me eventually. When that time comes, it will be the ultimate pleasure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Treats his fetch-boy as furniture — the warm bottle is thrown back at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y1v3-p111-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi","q":"ch 3  3 2  the warm water volleyball on the class c beach until ryuen calls him over to serve   i said to bring me cold water  this water s warm","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y1v3-p111-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the warm water<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.111–112<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volleyball on the Class C beach until Ryūen calls him over to serve.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I said to bring me cold water. This water&#x27;s warm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Rushes sweat-dripping to the tent and hands over a bottle; Ryūen pours it out and throws it back at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Ishizaki&#x27;s body stiffened.” at the snake-pupil hum; he picks the bottle up and runs back to the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  walking back from the class c shore on the path inland past the beach  he turns to scan the class c shore once more while the walk back is still arguing over what ryuen s spending means   the test is literally about freedom  ryuuen s way of thinking is one way to approach it  it seems like ibuki and another student rebelled  and because of that class c will lose twenty points a day  since he knew he d be losing that many points every day no matter what  he came up with a drastic strategy   since i didn t know when ryuuen had decided to spend all of class c s points  i could only guess   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him   a zero point strategy  huh  i see  that s really interesting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the path inland past the beach, he turns to scan the Class C shore once more while the walk back is still arguing over what Ryūen&#x27;s spending means.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “The test is literally about freedom. Ryuuen’s way of thinking is one way to approach it. It seems like Ibuki and another student rebelled, and because of that Class C will lose twenty points a day. Since he knew he’d be losing…”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “A zero-point strategy, huh? I see. That’s really interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The test is literally about freedom. Ryuuen’s way of thinking is one way to approach it. It seems like Ibuki and another student rebelled, and because of that Class C will lose twenty points a day. Since he knew he’d be losing that many points every day no matter what, he came up with a drastic strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Since I didn’t know when Ryuuen had decided to spend all of Class C’s points, I could only guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange is never tagged; her line is confirmed by the narration that follows it, and both of his stand as the remarks she answers.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads winning as more than saving the class&#x27;s own points: dissent inside the group would have to be silenced before a zero-points route could work.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 3  the walk back  and class b s camp walking inland from the class c shore  she is still arguing over ryuen s spending when the visit to class b s camp begins   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him   i was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship  like last time   yeah  there s a lot to make us uneasy right now  but we have to try and make it through   i was thinking that we should talk about that  too  if we didn t have to be on guard with even one class  we d really appreciate it  as long as you don t mind  ichinose san  i d like you to accept the proposal   this class has fallen in line far better than i could have imagined  i suppose that s because you re the one taking command  right   no  we do have a boy named hirata  though  everyone in class clusters around him   ichinose san  i m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions  but we want to confirm class a s status  can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp  even something you know about the area might really help   secretive  what kind of measures has class a taken   you can t use any sly tricks in this test  ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points  they might be having fun right now  but they re going to regret it later   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long   ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking inland from the Class C shore, she is still arguing over Ryūen&#x27;s spending when the visit to Class B&#x27;s camp begins.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship, like last time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yeah. There’s a lot to make us uneasy right now, but we have to try and make it through.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rejects the zero-points route on principle: points are to be won back, not written off.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Arrives as a visitor with Ayanokōji and declines the hammock offer, so Ichinose sits instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Listens through the whole tour — well, water shower, toilet, vinyl, heat — without interrupting.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Afterward lays out Class D&#x27;s situation completely, holding nothing back in the interest of fairness.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was thinking that we should talk about that, too. If we didn’t have to be on guard with even one class, we’d really appreciate it. As long as you don’t mind, Ichinose-san, I’d like you to accept the proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; she is the one addressing Ichinose by name, and Ichinose&#x27;s proposal and reply are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This class has fallen in line far better than I could have imagined. I suppose that’s because you’re the one taking command, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges Class B by its order: every student carrying out a role, and doing the duty happily, with nobody trying to skip out.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. We do have a boy named Hirata, though. Everyone in class clusters around him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him as the one Class D gathers around, then changes the topic.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ichinose-san. I’m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions, but we want to confirm Class A’s status. Can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp? Even something you know about the area might really help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Secretive? What kind of measures has Class A taken?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t use any sly tricks in this test. Ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points. They might be having fun right now, but they’re going to regret it later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; the narration that follows anchors the withheld withdrawal plan on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In general, I think we’re all on the same page, but they’re further ahead. I can’t deny it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Says it as a declaration of defeat: the distance between D and B is not only a matter of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 3  class b s camp at the well deep forest past the broken landmark tree  class b s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees  ichinose tying a cord  kanzaki sitting a little way off   well  i suppose it s just what we d expect from class b   your class seems to be functioning well  despite obstacles   i m sorry if we re getting in the way   what s a water shower  i m a little curious about that   did you already know about them  water showers  i mean   a class c student   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deep forest past the broken landmark tree: Class B&#x27;s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees, Ichinose tying a cord, Kanzaki sitting a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kaneda-satoru\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, I suppose it’s just what we’d expect from Class B…”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Your class seems to be functioning well, despite obstacles.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m sorry if we’re getting in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks instead of tents, and a path of student tracks already beaten through the forest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the broken tree as a landmark the school left on purpose, which is why Kanzaki&#x27;s directions needed no detail.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The three lines are untagged; Ichinose takes up and answers each of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She reads the visit as a request and welcomes them without any hint of protest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s a water shower? I’m a little curious about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Judges the water shower probably less effective than the temporary shower because it costs five points less, and passes on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you already know about them? Water showers, I mean,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Class B&#x27;s purchases itemize to exactly seventy points once the food is counted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets that total against Class D with Kōenji&#x27;s retirement already deducted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Weighs the foraging against the fruit Kushida&#x27;s group carried back for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Watches the Class B method in one pass: the well tested before anyone drinks, hot water on a gas can, unlimited vinyl sheets granted with the temporary toilet, and water sprinkled to pull the heat out of the soil.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He stays silent while she lays out Class D&#x27;s side and runs the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The visitors&#x27; questions about hard ground and the heat are never tagged and are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Names him as a Class C student before Ichinose can finish answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A Class C student?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Files him as the Class C boy who resisted Ryūen and was taken in by Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Says farewell with Horikita and leaves the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets Class D against Class B on the way out: Class D has selfish students like Kōenji who run off alone, and nobody with the power to step in.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow the departure are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kaneda-satoru ichinose-honami","q":"ch 3  3 3  the camp that already works class b s base around the well  she is tying a hammock cord to a tree when horikita and ayanokoji walk in  and kanzaki sits a little way off   huh  horikita san  and ayanokouji kun   ha ha  yeah  it was really difficult at first  but we tried a bunch of different things  and it worked out  though the list of chores just keeps on increasing  there s still a ton of work left   oh  i m sorry  that probably sounded like i was trying to drive you guys away  i think it s all right if you hang around for a while  you probably came here to ask me something  right   i think so  too   hammocks  cookware  small tent  lantern  and temporary toilet  fishing rod  a water shower  if we combine those items with the food we purchased  the total comes to exactly seventy points   well  let s go over the situation bit by bit  shall we  since there are various places in the woods where we can find fruits and vegetables  we can compensate for deficiencies in points by foraging for food  we can also head out to the sea and fish  that s what i was thinking we d do for food  we re not worried about water  since we have a well   at first we were worried whether the water was safe to drink    starting this morning  we had everyone use the   well to get water   also  there s enough natural water that we can use it for showers  that s what a water shower is   after we put water in the tank here  we get hot water in only a few seconds  it s really convenient  we use ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the camp that already works<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class B&#x27;s base around the well: she is tying a hammock cord to a tree when Horikita and Ayanokōji walk in, and Kanzaki sits a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kaneda-satoru\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Huh? Horikita-san? And Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ha ha, yeah. It was really difficult at first! But we tried a bunch of different things, and it worked out. Though the list of chores just keeps on increasing. There’s still a ton of work left,”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Oh, I’m sorry. That probably sounded like I was trying to drive you guys away. I think it’s all right if you hang around for a while. You probably came here to ask me something, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks strung for lack of tent space, unfamiliar equipment beside the water.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the interruption as a welcome rather than an intrusion: smiling, she assumes they came with a question.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Welcomes them without any hint of protest and invites them to sit on the hammock.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think so, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The agreement is untagged; it answers Horikita&#x27;s proposal directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hammocks. Cookware. Small tent, lantern, and temporary toilet. Fishing rod, a water shower… If we combine those items with the food we purchased, the total comes to exactly seventy points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Reads her class&#x27;s purchases aloud from a manual: seventy points in all.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, let’s go over the situation bit by bit, shall we? Since there are various places in the woods where we can find fruits and vegetables, we can compensate for deficiencies in points by foraging for food. We can also head out to the sea and fish. That’s what I was thinking we’d do for food. We’re not worried about water, since we have a well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Food comes from foraging and the sea; water comes from the well.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At first we were worried whether the water was safe to drink, … Starting this morning, we had everyone use the … well to get water.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Drinks from the well herself the day before, waits to see if she gets an upset stomach, and only then lets the class use it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, there’s enough natural water that we can use it for showers. That’s what a water shower is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After we put water in the tank here, we get hot water in only a few seconds. It’s really convenient. We use a gas can for the heat source. When we run out, I plan to request another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. This is the first I’ve heard about or used them. The school’s rules are rather scary, aren’t they? There weren’t any details in the manual, and we can’t ask the teacher, either. Thankfully we have some kids who are familiar with the outdoors in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We set up this temporary toilet instead of getting a shower room. We got it so that the people who dislike being seen by others when they shower could have privacy. The fabric is also waterproof.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, yeah. At first, I wondered what we were going to do, but then we took appropriate measures. Want a look?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lifts the tent flap after warning the girls inside and shows the vinyl sheets underfoot — about two centimeters thick.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we paid for the temporary toilet, we were told we had access to an unlimited number of vinyl sheets. So I might have asked for too many, but … we received a large number of them. Of course, I don’t want to waste resources, so I plan to put any unused vinyl sheets into one sheet, and return them in the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder if it’s because we sprinkle water around. We’ve sprinkled water near our beds, because they’re close to the well. We put some water in the plastic bottles that people drank from, and then everyone carries them around so they can sprinkle water efficiently. The water soaks into the soil quite easily, and since it takes some time for it to evaporate, the effect lingers and removes the heat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Beats the heat with sprinkled water rather than equipment — knowledge, not tools, is what makes the campsite work.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see… Having someone retire sounds like it really hurt you guys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, can we continue our cooperative relationship? I thought it would be a good idea to ignore the rule about trying to find out the leader’s identity. What do you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; the addressee anchors put these lines on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’m okay with that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reaffirms the cooperative relationship with her and agrees to drop the hunt for the leader&#x27;s identity.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. For the time being, anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the command credit only conditionally — for the time being.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Knows him from the soccer club and calls him really popular among the girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. From the soccer club! I know him, I know him! He’s really popular among the girls.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if you’re okay with something that might be useful, I can tell you something about their place. However, obtaining information is going to be tough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just after you cut through this area, there’s an opening. Turn right and go straight until you see a cave. That’s probably where the Class A base camp is. I went there myself to investigate, but I don’t know for sure. It’s because they’re so thoroughly defensive…or rather, secretive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has already scouted the Class A site herself and marks it as thoroughly defensive.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, seeing is believing. If you take a look yourselves, you’ll understand right away. Since you two are going to check on Class A, does that mean you already understand Class C’s situation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her assessment of Class C — no intention of taking the test seriously, five days left, no spot even looked for — runs untagged between her question and the narration that follows; it is left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Takes his interruption patiently, tells him where Nakanishi is, and sends him after Chihiro-chan&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think Nakanishi-kun headed down to the shore. Why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh no, not at all. I’m really happy you feel that way, Kaneda-kun. Can you head over and follow Chihiro-chan’s group? If you tell them I told you to do so, it’ll be okay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know him? It looks like he had some kind of dispute with Class C. He said he’d get by on his own, but I couldn’t just leave him. I haven’t asked him about his situation yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes in a Class C boy nobody else would take because she couldn&#x27;t just leave him — and has not yet asked him what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hardens when she hears that Ibuki was hit — the narration calls it strengthening her resolve to protect her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Closes the visit with farewells after the full exchange of information.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp with the Class B pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 3  3 3  at his own camp while class d visits sitting a little way off from ichinose when class d walks into the class b camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: at his own camp while Class D visits<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117, p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sitting a little way off from Ichinose when Class D walks into the Class B camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He says nothing during the visit; the pages place him in the background of the scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji credits him with having deduced Class D&#x27;s spending from what he saw at the river that morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The camp Class D found from his directions is hers; he stays out of the exchange while she runs it.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the river meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp with Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kaneda-satoru-y1v3-p124-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru kaneda-satoru","q":"ch 3  3 3  the class c boy who offers to help at class b s camp he interrupts ichinose in a reserved voice while horikita and ayanokoji are still there   pardon me  ichinose san  i m sorry to interrupt  do you know where nakanishi kun is   i thought i d offer to help  is that unnecessary   okay  thank you very much","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kaneda-satoru-y1v3-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.3: the Class C boy who offers to help<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.124<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kaneda-satoru\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Class B&#x27;s camp he interrupts Ichinose in a reserved voice while Horikita and Ayanokōji are still there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> “Pardon me, Ichinose-san? I’m sorry to interrupt. Do you know where Nakanishi-kun is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> “I thought I’d offer to help. Is that unnecessary?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> “Okay. Thank you very much!”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> A Class C student estranged from his class for resisting Ryūen and sheltered by Class B; Horikita notices that he speaks to Ichinose with unusual formality.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Asks her for work, and she sends him to follow Chihiro-chan&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The dispute with Ryūen that got him out of Class C; the pages say he claimed he would get by on his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He has not told anyone his situation yet, and Ichinose says she has not asked him.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 4  the class a cave the cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon s mouth  with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside  he steps over horikita and walks up to it   let s go  i mean  it s class a  so of course we re going to be scared  there s nothing we can do about that   and what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot  we can barely see  and there s no one around  there s not much we can see unless we enter the cave   i haven t thought of anything  come on  don t worry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon&#x27;s mouth, with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside; he steps over Horikita and walks up to it.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Let’s go. I mean, it’s Class A, so of course we’re going to be scared. There’s nothing we can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “And what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot? We can barely see, and there’s no one around. There’s not much we can see unless we enter the cave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I haven’t thought of anything. Come on, don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class A site: a cave in the mountainside, its entrance hidden behind vinyl sheets joined into one giant tarp.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Goes up openly rather than scouting from cover so that he can see inside — and finds the tarp already blocking the view.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening line on the approach is untagged; Horikita&#x27;s two questions are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Recognizes Yahiko as one of the two who found the cave on the first day; Katsuragi is away.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The closing judgment — that Class A has to be left alone and cannot be investigated — is his, left untagged and recorded here without a quotation.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 4  talking past class a at the cave she and ayanokoji walk up to the class a cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything   what are you planning  we gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves   we came to snoop  you have a problem   i mean  i would ve thought that since you re in class a you d be clever  but   well  rather than clever  i d say you re underhanded  what cowardly methods   i m horikita  from class d   stupid  huh  in that case  there s no harm in us seeing what s inside  right  or does that make you feel uncomfortable   so it s not a problem if we look  you re in the way   we re just going to look inside  that itself isn t a violation of the rules  right   oh  so you occupy this place  i didn t know that  is there a device inside   well  there definitely aren t any rules that say we can t go into the cave  it s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it s being occupied  but that s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything  we should have the right to look inside  or at least to verify if there s equipment  right  if we couldn t do that  then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot  that s not what this test is about   you re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot  the rules don t protect such actions   well  fine  i look forward to seeing the results  and class a s abilities","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Ayanokōji walk up to the Class A cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What are you planning? We gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We came to snoop. You have a problem?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I mean, I would’ve thought that since you’re in Class A you’d be clever, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The approach dialogue is untagged; the question-and-answer chain, and the question tagged to her at the end of it, put these on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Switches into a deliberate provocation — the narration calls it a daring switch flipped in her brain.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, rather than clever, I’d say you’re underhanded. What cowardly methods.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Horikita, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stupid, huh? In that case, there’s no harm in us seeing what’s inside, right? Or does that make you feel uncomfortable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it’s not a problem if we look? You’re in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re just going to look inside. That itself isn’t a violation of the rules, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? So you occupy this place. I didn’t know that. Is there a device inside?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Provokes him on purpose and talks past every block he puts up.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there definitely aren’t any rules that say we can’t go into the cave. It’s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it’s being occupied, but that’s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything. We should have the right to look inside, or at least to verify if there’s equipment, right? If we couldn’t do that, then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot. That’s not what this test is about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The monopoly argument: occupation bars use, not looking, and a spot that nobody may inspect could be seized by anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot. The rules don’t protect such actions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Both p.128 lines are untagged; the second is answered by Katsuragi conceding the point.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Matched and stopped by his unspoken-rule argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fine. I look forward to seeing the results, and Class A’s abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Leaves with the wind knocked out of her; without Katsuragi&#x27;s arrival she would have gone through the vinyl.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her mutters “W-wait.” and “Ugh, what an unintelligible, half-assed answer.” are untagged; the second answers his own admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko","q":"ch 3  3 4  holding the entrance at the class a cave entrance as class d approaches  the two temporary toilets and the shower room stand outside   who are you guys  what class are you from   what   hah  it s obvious you re from class d  you re a bunch of stupid failures  after all   that s not it at all   w wait  hey  wait  i said  don t just do whatever you please   stop screwing around  class a occupies this spot  class d doesn t have permission to use it   y yeah  so back off   huh   katsuragi san  these two came to snoop around our camp  they re a bunch of filthy losers   s sorry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: holding the entrance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the Class A cave entrance as Class D approaches; the two temporary toilets and the shower room stand outside.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Who are you guys? What class are you from?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Hah, it’s obvious you’re from Class D. You’re a bunch of stupid failures, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Identified as the one of the pair who found the cave quickly on the first day.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not it at all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait! Hey! Wait, I said! Don’t just do whatever you please!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Moves in front of Horikita to block her path.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop screwing around. Class A occupies this spot. Class D doesn’t have permission to use it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-yeah. So back off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi-san! These two came to snoop around our camp! They’re a bunch of filthy losers!”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Irritated by her provocation and unable to stop her; she talks past every objection he makes.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Takes the rebuke — his answer to the provocation was exactly the bait it was meant to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Left holding the entrance alone when Katsuragi is away; the sharp one of the pair is absent until the end of the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the second man in the cave<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the second meeting at the thicket<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 3  3 4  the parley at the cave named first as absent from the class a cave  then arriving at the entrance midway through the standoff with horikita   what are you doing  i don t recall giving you permission to invite guests   well then  it should be fine for you to look inside  however  prepare yourself  the moment you touch anything  i will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class  i can t guarantee what will happen to class d as a result   you re right about that  i cannot argue the point  however  it s something of an unspoken rule  you in class d have a spot by the river  class b has a well  you live in and surround the occupied space  so it s halfway monopolized  have you taken any forceful measures in dealing with trespassers to your area   one class occupies one spot  then  they continue to protect that spot so they may obtain points until the end of the test  if you violate this unspoken rule  it creates chaos  naturally  class a will trespass upon class d s base in retaliation  we should avoid trouble   we are quite capable  we also expect things from you  class d  by which i mean  your futile struggling","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.127–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named first as absent from the Class A cave, then arriving at the entrance midway through the standoff with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “What are you doing? I don’t recall giving you permission to invite guests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Well then, it should be fine for you to look inside. However, prepare yourself. The moment you touch anything, I will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class. I can’t guarantee what will…”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You’re right about that. I cannot argue the point. However, it’s something of an unspoken rule. You in Class D have a spot by the river. Class B has a well. You live in and surround the occupied space, so it’s halfway…”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page introduces him as the sharp-witted one of the pair who found the cave on the first day.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, it should be fine for you to look inside. However, prepare yourself. The moment you touch anything, I will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class. I can’t guarantee what will happen to Class D as a result.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Threatens a school report over touched vinyl — read as probably bluffing, with some genuine danger behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right about that. I cannot argue the point. However, it’s something of an unspoken rule. You in Class D have a spot by the river. Class B has a well. You live in and surround the occupied space, so it’s halfway monopolized. Have you taken any forceful measures in dealing with trespassers to your area?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Concedes the formal point and answers it with practice: every class already defends its own area.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “One class occupies one spot. Then, they continue to protect that spot so they may obtain points until the end of the test. If you violate this unspoken rule, it creates chaos. Naturally, Class A will trespass upon Class D’s base in retaliation. We should avoid trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> States the island&#x27;s working rule: one spot per class, held for the whole test, or retaliation follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We are quite capable. We also expect things from you, Class D. By which I mean, your futile struggling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Pulls his partner off the provocation: answer bait like that and the other side backs down.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ends her advance with words; the narration has her stopped in her tracks by his calm.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> With him on the entrance, Class D&#x27;s only option is retreat — he has stripped every other one away.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Class A leader who showed his card<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the cornfield offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 4  4 1  the walk with sakura third day  before noon  he slips out of base camp alone for the forest entrance to see what kouenji had been looking at  and sakura catches up  out of breath   didn t i tie a handkerchief around a tree  anyway  i thought i d just go and check something out   isn t it better for you to stay back  won t it bother you if people start spreading rumors   it s not going to be particularly easy  right  i mean  after we went through all the trouble of coming to this island  i think you should have a little fun  though i m not one to talk about fun  myself   well then  how about we go together  but i have a condition  if we get into trouble later  you won t blame yourself  okay   are you getting along well with the other girls  i mean  you can t really do things alone in this test  right   that s not true  you re making progress  sakura chan   it is true  maybe you can t see it  but you re definitely making progress little by little   it s okay  you ll make some friends really soon  sakura  then school will become much more fun   that reminds me  that guy  from the incident before it seems like he resigned   i didn t really do anything  you were saved because you got close to kushida  and because horikita and ichinose helped out  i was just a bystander  anyway  more importantly  nothing else weird has happened  right   besides  even though you usually act nervous  you always had this really confident expression when you were an idol   a long time ago  b","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.131–135<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third day, before noon: he slips out of base camp alone for the forest entrance to see what Kouenji had been looking at, and Sakura catches up, out of breath.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Didn’t I tie a handkerchief around a tree? Anyway, I thought I’d just go and check something out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Isn’t it better for you to stay back? Won’t it bother you if people start spreading rumors?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s not going to be particularly easy, right? I mean, after we went through all the trouble of coming to this island, I think you should have a little fun… Though I’m not one to talk about fun, myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The forest path out of base camp, marked by a handkerchief tied around a tree.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line just above the quoted one prints “didn’t had the time”; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Turns her request down with that excuse — she answers that this is fun, crouches and hides her face, and he takes her along after all.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts her company on one condition: if they get into trouble later, she must not blame herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, how about we go together? But I have a condition. If we get into trouble later, you won’t blame yourself. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you getting along well with the other girls? I mean, you can’t really do things alone in this test, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not true. You’re making progress, Sakura-chan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It is true. Maybe you can’t see it, but you’re definitely making progress little by little.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s okay. You’ll make some friends really soon, Sakura. Then school will become much more fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Appeals from the bottom of his heart for the first time, choosing words and attitude together; the narration judges it the right method for someone who lacks confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her lines carry the narration tags or address him by name; his replies through the walk are untagged and recorded here.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That reminds me… That guy, from the incident before…it seems like he resigned.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t really do anything. You were saved because you got close to Kushida, and because Horikita and Ichinose helped out. I was just a bystander. Anyway, more importantly, nothing else weird has happened, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Credits Kushida’s proximity and Horikita and Ichinose’s help with the stalker affair; his own part was bystander only.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, even though you usually act nervous, you always had this really confident expression when you were an idol.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A long time ago? But when you were featured in magazines you probably didn’t take the pictures yourself, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Draws her out on the idol years until she describes erasing herself to endure the shoots; the narration reads her as scarred by the stalker but headed in a better direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Considering even Kouenji’s satisfaction, the school has probably been really good about keeping up the place. Normally, an overseas jungle would be more dangerous.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Rests with her against one tree half an hour up the steep trail — the longest time alone with her since the landing — and reads the distance between them shortening toward friendship, the first relationship he has felt tilt that way.<span class=\"pg\">p.134–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if I’m in the picture, wouldn’t that spoil the scenery?”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Watching her frame the shot with thumb and forefingers: “Preserving memories, huh? So that was why Ibuki had a digital camera.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His inference rather than a fact about Ibuki: her reason for carrying a camera at school is applied to the Class C girl.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"ch 4  4 1  chasing him into the forest chases him out of base camp breathless on the third day and insists on coming along  rumors or not   ahh  ahh  ahh  wh where are you planning to go now  ayanokouji kun   i it s probably not okay for me to come along  is it  i d only slow you down  probably  but   that doesn t bother me at all  besides  i   th this is fun  though   really  it s okay   no  not at all  we don t really talk or anything   i m just worthless  really  i can t do sports  or study  i m not really growing as a person in any area   huh  me  progress  ah ha ha  that s not true  though   thank you for everything  everything worked out thanks to you  ayanokouji kun   no  everything s been fine  actually  i ve been taking a little break from the bulletin board  too   well  that s that s because i did the photography myself   i didn t do well  and i also took way more time than the others  a cameraman would take pictures of the girls to make sure there were as few people involved as possible  besides back then  i was able to bear it because i made myself empty  it was like i erased myself  eliminated my feelings  but i eventually reached my limit  so i had to take a break   nature sure is amazing  isn t it  i like to spend a lot of my free time out in nature  even if it s just walking around   when we left for the trip  i felt depressed at first  i didn t have any friends  and i don t really like traveling  i thought it would be fine if i could just stay in my room  if ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: chasing him into the forest<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.131–135<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chases him out of base camp breathless on the third day and insists on coming along, rumors or not.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Ahh, ahh, ahh… Wh-where are you planning to go now, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “I-It’s probably not okay for me…to come along, is it? I’d only slow you down, probably, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “That doesn’t bother me at all. Besides, I….”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Th-this is fun, though!”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Offers more resistance to being left behind than he expects; after their eyes meet she crouches and hides her face.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? It’s okay?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, not at all… We don’t really talk or anything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m just worthless, really. I can’t do sports, or study. I’m not really growing as a person in any area.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Me, progress? Ah ha ha… That’s not true, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Absolute self-devaluation — worthless, no growth in any area — delivered while twirling her hair with an index finger, with a laugh to wave off the encouragement.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Stops walking at his assurance, eyes trembling, to work out whether he means it.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you for everything… Everything worked out thanks to you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, everything’s been fine. Actually, I’ve been taking a little break from the bulletin board, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The stalker from the electronics store has resigned, and she has stepped back from the bulletin board as a precaution.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s…that’s because I did the photography myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t do well, and I also took way more time than the others. A cameraman would take pictures of the girls to make sure there were as few people involved as possible. Besides…back then, I was able to bear it because I made myself empty. It was like I erased myself, eliminated my feelings. But I eventually reached my limit, so I had to take a break.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> On the idol years: she made herself empty to get through the shoots and only broke when she reached her limit — spoken in one run, stopping at the end for a deep breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The trip answer and the lines between the narration beats are untagged; they continue her own tagged speech, so they are recorded as hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nature sure is amazing, isn’t it? I like to spend a lot of my free time out in nature, even if it’s just walking around,”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we left for the trip, I felt depressed at first. I didn’t have any friends, and I don’t really like traveling. I thought it would be fine if I could just stay in my room. If I did that, my life would have been the same as always. But then, all this happened. We were told this was some kind of test…”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But now I’m kind of glad that we came here. That’s because I never really had the chance to talk with you like this before, Ayanokouji-kun…”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The two of them deep in the forest, embraced by nature and a feeling of serenity.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wish we could stay like this forever…”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh… It’s too bad. If I had my digital camera, I probably could have taken the best photos, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, if you’re in the picture, Ayanokouji-kun, it will be the best photo… Ah! No! I mean, that is, I’ve never taken a picture with a friend before!”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Frames herself and him with thumb and forefingers several times, then makes an embarrassed face at having done it.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The camera habit runs deep enough to frame a shot that cannot be taken — and the new thing she names is a picture with a friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the forest team, the blush, and the second volunteer shift<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 4  4 2  the caterpillar and the corn a hairy caterpillar drops into sakura s hair during the break  pointing it out might make her scream it into her clothes  so he has to remove it without telling her   sakura  there s something i want to ask you   you are you okay with bugs   yeah  bugs  like grasshoppers and dragonflies  those kinds of things   i see  well  all right then   hmm  anyway  don t move for the time being  okay   for the time being  let s investigate the area  but don t go too far  then let s check on each other regularly  if we don t concentrate  it s likely we ll get distracted   did you notice something   so  this is what kouenji saw   sorry  sorry  i thought it would be okay  wait  what did you mean by  it s too soon   if we tie up the openings of my shirt  we can use it as a bag  that way  we could carry more at once","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.137–140<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A hairy caterpillar drops into Sakura’s hair during the break; pointing it out might make her scream it into her clothes, so he has to remove it without telling her.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sakura, there’s something I want to ask you…”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You…are you okay with bugs?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah. Bugs. Like grasshoppers and dragonflies, those kinds of things”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, all right then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. Anyway, don’t move for the time being, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Feigns a casual interest in bugs to learn what she can stand, then holds off acting until he has another way.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reaches through his own revulsion — a city boy who hates insects — touches the caterpillar off her hair and throws it into the bushes; she never learns what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, let’s investigate the area, but don’t go too far. Then let’s check on each other regularly. If we don’t concentrate, it’s likely we’ll get distracted.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you notice something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> About twenty minutes from base camp by the handkerchief marker: the rise where Kouenji had stood.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finds nothing by sight, then works the soil, the roots, the leaves and the air with all five senses.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, this is what Kouenji saw…”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the soil color under the corn and the weed cover around it as artificial cultivation — proof that school officials come and go on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration answers Kouenji’s silent gaze from the second day: he saw the corn at first glance and said nothing out of pride.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, sorry. I thought it would be okay. Wait, what did you mean by ‘it’s too soon’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we tie up the openings of my shirt, we can use it as a bag. That way… we could carry more at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Turns his shirt into a carry bag rather than leave the ears behind for another class to harvest while they are away.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bags line that opens the harvest is untagged — either speaker fits — and is left as an attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"ch 4  4 2  the caterpillar and the corn panics when he seizes her shoulders mid break   a caterpillar is in her hair  a fact he never tells her   wh what  what is it   wh what is it   n not at all  i absolutely can t stand them  ants either   o okay  sure   ugh i feel like there was something gross on me   umm  what s different   hey  look  i found something amazing   huh  wh wh wh what are you doing  ayanokouji kun  it s way too soon for that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.137–140<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Panics when he seizes her shoulders mid-break — a caterpillar is in her hair, a fact he never tells her.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Wh-what?! What is it?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “Wh-what is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “N-not at all. I absolutely can’t stand them. Ants either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “O-okay. Sure…”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ugh…I feel like there was something gross on me…”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm… What’s different?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Searches the bushes away from him and shrieks at something in them.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, look! I found something amazing!”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Finds a different variety of leaves and yellow ears inside a thicket — the discovery the trip was for.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?! Wh-wh-wh-what are you doing, Ayanokouji-kun?! It’s way too soon for that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drops the corn and covers her eyes with both hands when he takes his shirt off.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: chasing him into the forest<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei sakura-airi ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 4  4 3  katsuragi at the cornfield katsuragi and yahiko arrive at the thicket while sakura is staring at the corn   i m ayanokouji  from class d  this is sakura   there s nothing we can do  there s only the two of us here   we appreciate the offer  but our class told us to be careful  they ll get mad if they find out we relied on class a for help  i m sorry  but we have to decline   in that case  i d have no choice but to give up what i m carrying right now   calm down  this is a misunderstanding  that s all  we didn t do  anything   i have to go talk with hirata  sorry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi and Yahiko arrive at the thicket while Sakura is staring at the corn.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m Ayanokouji, from Class D. This is Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “There’s nothing we can do. There’s only the two of us here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “We appreciate the offer, but our class told us to be careful. They’ll get mad if they find out we relied on Class A for help. I’m sorry, but we have to decline.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Recognized as the spy from yesterday — the second time the pair has met him.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Refuses the partnership with a fabricated class order — the narration marks the reason a lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, I’d have no choice but to give up what I’m carrying right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Answers the watch-offer by abandoning the spot rather than accepting help; Katsuragi withdraws without force.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Leaves with her while she still looks worried, Katsuragi’s intentions unread.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Back at base camp, Ike’s greeting brings Yamauchi running over.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Meets the shirtless-with-Sakura accusation with a deflection, then leaves it unanswered.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down. This is a misunderstanding, that’s all. We didn’t do… anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have to go talk with Hirata. Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Leaves Yamauchi’s rant to give Hirata the report; soon afterward a team is organized and the class works the cornfield.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The bag comes back full by one o’clock, and the spot stays under Katsuragi’s eye — good or bad intentions left unknown.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The camp’s closing exchanges — the full bag, Katsuragi being nearby — are untagged and left as attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi totsuka-yahiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 4  4 3  the cornfield offer arrives with yahiko at the thicket while sakura is staring at the corn  apologizes for the surprise   i m sorry  we didn t mean to surprise you  he had no bad intentions  either  please forgive us   my name s katsuragi  from class a  he s yahiko  since this is the second time we ve met  a self introduction should be fine  yes   you found this  don t worry  we have no intention of snatching it away from you  but if someone else finds this spot  they ll likely take it away   you re the one who doesn t seem to understand the situation  yahiko  don t dismiss the danger of moving through the forest alone  it s difficult enough in groups of men  but when men and women are together  no matter what  there will be certain limitations to what you can do   we ll help you   i see  we can t force you  however  can you trust us  after you leave here  there s a chance we ll make off with all of this  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the cornfield offer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives with Yahiko at the thicket while Sakura is staring at the corn; apologizes for the surprise.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I’m sorry. We didn’t mean to surprise you. He had no bad intentions, either. Please forgive us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “My name’s Katsuragi, from Class A. He’s Yahiko. Since this is the second time we’ve met, a self-introduction should be fine, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You found this. Don’t worry, we have no intention of snatching it away from you. But if someone else finds this spot, they’ll likely take it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Apologizes for startling her — he has seen where she ran to behind his back.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the one who doesn’t seem to understand the situation, Yahiko. Don’t dismiss the danger of moving through the forest alone. It’s difficult enough in groups of men, but when men and women are together, no matter what, there will be certain limitations to what you can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Will not go into the forest alone — groups of men already strain, mixed company more; the narration gives it as the reason he never went alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. We can’t force you. However, can you trust us? After you leave here, there’s a chance we’ll make off with all of this, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Silences his objections with a look after the head-thump; partnership is offered over his visible refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The offer and the trust-question both land on him; he refuses the first and gives up the spot rather than accept the second, and Katsuragi withdraws without force.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Offer refused, he pivots to asking to be trusted instead — then quietly clears a path for them.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays at the corn after they leave so their harvest runs under his eye; whether that was good or bad intent is left open.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class A now knows the spot and watches it from close by.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"ch 4  4 3  katsuragi at the cornfield jumps when katsuragi and yahiko arrive at the thicket and hides behind his back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p140-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Jumps when Katsuragi and Yahiko arrive at the thicket and hides behind his back.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Back at base camp for the report; the harvest team forms soon after and everyone is back by one o’clock.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Draws his apology for the surprise — he saw where she had run to.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> His shout makes her jump again and curl into a ball; Katsuragi answers with a thump to his head.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike’s camp greeting names her as one of the two who found the food.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The jealousy scene runs over her: he shoves Ayanokōji away from her side before the whole camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Leaves the thicket with him while she still looks worried.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko","q":"ch 4  4 3  the second meeting at the thicket arrives with katsuragi at the corn thicket  his first words are about the food   wow  look  katsuragi san  there s an incredible amount of food here   hey  you re the spy from yesterday   you idiots  one of you two can stay behind and watch the stuff  isn t that right  katsuragi san   a are you serious  katsuragi san  but  working together with class d is","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p140-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the second meeting at the thicket<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–141<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives with Katsuragi at the corn thicket; his first words are about the food.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Wow. Look, Katsuragi-san! There’s an incredible amount of food here!”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Hey, you’re the spy from yesterday!”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “You idiots. One of you two can stay behind and watch the stuff! Isn’t that right, Katsuragi-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Apologizes in low spirits under Katsuragi’s stern look.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recognizes him as the spy from yesterday — the second time the two have met.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> His shout makes her jump and curl into a ball behind his back.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A-are you serious, Katsuragi-san? But, working together with Class D is—”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Wants to refuse Class D outright and stays quiet only after the sharp look; his watch idea is overridden by the offer to help.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: holding the entrance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p141-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki ike-kanji","q":"ch 4  4 3  the camp greeting at base camp when the pair comes back from the forest   what an amazing find  ayanokouji  you too  sakura  let s go get it  yamauchi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p141-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p141-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the camp greeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.141<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At base camp when the pair comes back from the forest.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “What an amazing find, Ayanokouji! You too, Sakura! Let’s go get it, Yamauchi!”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Greets him as the finder of the food, before the class knows what has been found.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Names her as the second finder in the same shout.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The shout is what sends him sprinting over — and into the jealousy scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: the chips at his feet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 4  4 3  the shirtless accusation dashes over when ike calls  grabs his arm and shoves him away from sakura   h h hey  you  why were you all alone and shirtless with sakura  why  huh   i trusted you  ayanokouji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p141-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the shirtless accusation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.141–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dashes over when Ike calls, grabs his arm and shoves him away from Sakura.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “H-h-hey, you! Why were you all alone and shirtless with Sakura?! Why?! Huh?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “I trusted you, Ayanokouji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The whole challenge is the pairing — he puts himself between them in front of the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Answers the call straight into the rant.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Rants and raves while he goes off to report to Hirata; the accusation is never answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0–§2.8: the target-switch, the matches, and bringing Ibuki in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 3  the corn report at base camp when ayanokoji cuts out of yamauchi s rant to reach him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\">Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At base camp when Ayanokōji cuts out of Yamauchi’s rant to reach him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets the corn report first-hand; soon afterward students are organized into a team that brings the harvest back.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 5  the solo sweep toward class a fourth day  laughter has replaced complaint   corn  fish and fruit have the class ahead   when he borrows a ballpoint pen  takes his folded map and walks out of base camp   so  you won t occupy this spot out of more than a sense of prudence   i m ayanokouji  from class d   give it back   i can t say   i can t say  if i did i may not be able to return to my class   you re asking for me to sell out my class for money   sorry  but i don t believe it  how would you pay someone  we don t   have any cell phones here  right   a memorandum  huh  let me ask you something for my own reference  can you tell me how many points i d get if i did tell you something   could i have someone trustworthy settle things  for example  someone like katsuragi  or perhaps sa   i ve heard rumors that katsuragi is class a s representative","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\">Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.144–148<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fourth day: laughter has replaced complaint — corn, fish and fruit have the class ahead — when he borrows a ballpoint pen, takes his folded map and walks out of base camp.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “So, you won’t occupy this spot out of more than a sense of prudence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m Ayanokouji, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Give it back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> About 100 points spent in total, Kōenji&#x27;s retirement included; at this pace the class ends the test with points left over, and even Yukimura has no complaints.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Breaks the test down 80:20 — eighty percent defensive cooperation, twenty percent offensive scouting — with the smaller share deciding outcomes the more.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the balance as meaning Class D now has to attack the other classes, and sets out for Class A&#x27;s area around the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The cliff below the cave: a ladder in a blind spot drops to a hut spot with fishing tackle.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Recalls the facilities seen from the ship, finds the ladder anyone would miss at first glance, and marks the hut&#x27;s approximate position on his map.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The hut spot means fish without borrowing equipment; the device shows Class A occupying with four hours remaining, and the dusty tools show the gear itself has not been used.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the unoccupied tower as deliberate — holding a visible facility risks observation, and Katsuragi is too cautious for bait this sweet and this close.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; it voices his reading of the empty tower a moment before the ambush and is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Two Class A boys spring the trap — one checks the terminal for a fresh claim, one puts a branch to his throat — and the search takes his pen and folded map.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say. If I did…I may not be able to return to my class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Holds the line through a rapid-fire interrogation — three seconds, four seconds of silence — without naming anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The offer on the table — “There’s one more thing I talk to you about. If you tell us the identity of your leader, we’re prepared to offer a generous reward. 100,000 or 200,000 points.” — first-come, first-serve, signed by memorandum and paid after the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re asking for me to sell out my class for money?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I don’t believe it. How would you pay someone? We don’t … have any cell phones here, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A memorandum, huh? Let me ask you something for my own reference… Can you tell me how many points I’d get if I did tell you something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could I have someone trustworthy settle things? For example, someone like Katsuragi. Or perhaps Sa—”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Drops Katsuragi&#x27;s name as bait of his own — cut off at “Sa—”, the sentence buys the reaction he was after.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve heard rumors that Katsuragi is Class A’s representative.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Their correction — “Don’t make me laugh. Sakayanagi is the representative of Class A. Not Katsuragi. You can go now.” — marks the pair as Katsuragi&#x27;s enemies and puts who really leads Class A in question.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 5  5 1  the ghost camp and the class a question at the emptied class c beach   yesterday s carnival now a ghost town   when ichinose and kanzaki arrive behind him   i m in charge of finding food  i was searching around the forest  and ended up here   i just happened to hear a little bit about this  but do katsuragi and sakayanagi in class a have opposing groups   oh  nothing  horikita just gave me an order  she said if i had time  to go and find out something  she wondered if this would be our chance to get back at class a  well  even though it s said they quarrel intensely  i imagine they ll come together during the test   i see  well  i ll tell horikita later  ah jeez  she told me to investigate on my own  she gets flustered working with others  well please pretend that you didn t hear that last part  it s going to be bothersome if she gets angry with me   it s about time for me to look for food  they ll be angry if i return empty handed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\">Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.149–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the emptied Class C beach — yesterday&#x27;s carnival now a ghost town — when Ichinose and Kanzaki arrive behind him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m in charge of finding food. I was searching around the forest, and ended up here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I just happened to hear a little bit about this, but do Katsuragi and Sakayanagi in Class A have opposing groups?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Oh, nothing. Horikita just gave me an order. She said if I had time, to go and find out something. She wondered if this would be our chance to get back at Class A. Well, even though it’s said they quarrel intensely, I imagine…”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His replies through the visit are untagged POV lines; the pair&#x27;s strategy exchange runs untagged too, and only their addressee- or narration-anchored lines are recorded on their pages — the rest are listed with the chapter&#x27;s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Hides with the pair in the shade, takes her midday warning, and thanks her for the parting caution.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, nothing. Horikita just gave me an order. She said if I had time, to go and find out something. She wondered if this would be our chance to get back at Class A. Well, even though it’s said they quarrel intensely, I imagine they’ll come together during the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Puts the Class A question to him and Ichinose; what comes back is the pair’s shared account, untagged between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Puts the questions in Horikita&#x27;s mouth so that his own interest in Class A&#x27;s split is not what the pair remember.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, I’ll tell Horikita later. Ah jeez, she told me to investigate on my own. She gets flustered working with others. Well…please pretend that you didn’t hear that last part. It’s going to be bothersome if she gets angry with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about time for me to look for food. They’ll be angry if I return empty-handed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p149-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ch 5  5 1  the ghost camp with the class b pair arrives behind him at the emptied class c beach with kanzaki  following the same curiosity about the silent camp   even though it s the middle of the day  i think it s dangerous to be running around alone   oh wow  there s no one around anymore  it s just like you said  kanzaki kun  seems like their strategy was to retire   well  rather than coming together  i think sakayanagi san is taking it easy during the test  that s why everyone thinks katsuragi kun is the leader  right   yeah  that seems like it s true  but wouldn t the students working under sakayanagi san be really unhappy  i mean  those two are complete opposite types  i would imagine their opinions would be clearly different  too   liberal and conservative  offense and defense  persecute and protect  those kinds of things  that s why they always seem to be clashing with each other  it s scary to think about class a going all out in that situation  if they managed to come together  class a would really demonstrate their true powers   well  let s both be careful not to get hurt  please don t do anything reckless","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p149-1\">Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp with the Class B pair<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.149–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives behind him at the emptied Class C beach with Kanzaki, following the same curiosity about the silent camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Even though it’s the middle of the day, I think it’s dangerous to be running around alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Oh wow, there’s no one around anymore. It’s just like you said, Kanzaki-kun. Seems like their strategy was to retire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, rather than coming together, I think Sakayanagi-san is taking it easy during the test. That’s why everyone thinks Katsuragi-kun is the leader. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The pair’s two arrival lines are untagged voices — either could be speaking — and both are left with the chapter’s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hides in the shade with Kanzaki to observe the state Class C was left in, and sighs in disappointment at the empty space.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The points-and-strategy exchange after that runs untagged through the three of them; nothing is assigned from turn order.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That seems like it’s true. But wouldn’t the students working under Sakayanagi-san be really unhappy? I mean, those two are complete opposite types. I would imagine their opinions would be clearly different, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The list that follows answers an untagged prompt — “Complete opposites?” — left between Kanzaki and Ayanokōji; it is recorded as hers because it continues the claim she had just made.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Liberal and conservative? Offense and defense? Persecute and protect? Those kinds of things. That’s why they always seem to be clashing with each other. It’s scary to think about Class A going all out in that situation. If they managed to come together, Class A would really demonstrate their true powers.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Poses the Sakayanagi reading as a question, takes his confirmation, and works the opposite-types idea through with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Warns him off midday wandering alone, trades the Class A reading openly, and keeps the Horikita order quiet when he asks.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Hides nothing of her class’s view — the pair explain their read of Class A to him outright while he hides his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.150–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, let’s both be careful not to get hurt. Please don’t do anything reckless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The closing reply to his request for secrecy — “Ha ha, don’t worry, we’ll keep it secret…” — is untagged between the pair; left with the gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the camp that already works<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p149-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 5  5 1  the ghost camp with ichinose arrives with ichinose at the emptied class c camp to read the same ghost town   katsuragi is a clever guy  but even though sakayanagi isn t around  there probably won t be anyone under her who ll put up resistance  they probably wouldn t do anything to deliberately cause a rift  there wouldn t be any merit in doing so","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p149-1\">Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp with Ichinose<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.149–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives with Ichinose at the emptied Class C camp to read the same ghost town.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Katsuragi is a clever guy. But even though Sakayanagi isn’t around, there probably won’t be anyone under her who’ll put up resistance. They probably wouldn’t do anything to deliberately cause a rift. There wouldn’t be any merit…”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Part of the pair that answers his Class A question with the account that Sakayanagi and Katsuragi quarrel and would see no merit in a rift.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer to his Class A question, the Class C points block and the strategy verdicts run untagged between the three; left with the chapter’s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Confirms her Sakayanagi reading when she poses it as a question, and checks his wristwatch to end the visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.150–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi is a clever guy. But even though Sakayanagi isn’t around, there probably won’t be anyone under her who’ll put up resistance. They probably wouldn’t do anything to deliberately cause a rift. There wouldn’t be any merit in doing so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Checks his wristwatch and suggests to Ichinose that they head back.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: at his own camp while Class D visits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 5  5 2  the faculty room deal flashback to the first semester s closing ceremonies  chabashira calls him to the faculty room the moment homeroom ends  before summer vacation can start   i don t remember doing anything   why did you sound all sarcastic   where do you think  i got called over by the teacher  so i don t really have a choice   don t say such nonsense   i don t understand why you called me over   so what did you want to talk to me about  i m busy planning my summer vacation right now   no  no  i was exaggerating when i said that  i have at least a few friends   before that  should we have tea  you must be thirsty   another abstract question  i see  is it okay if i say i think you re beautiful   umm  well  if you don t mind being compared to other teachers  i   think you don t care at all about class d s future  and that you re a cold   teacher with no interest in her students  that s my answer   i must say that s surprising  i would ve thought you were more capable  chabashira sensei   i m guessing someone made a trivial mistake  right   i m not catching your drift  what does this have to do with me   what am i supposed to say to that  you re joking  right   he said to expel me  well  that s nonsense  i don t know who it was  but you ignored his request and won t have me expelled  right   i m sorry  but i don t intend to do anything   are you threatening me   can i go now  i won t listen to any more of this   you ll probably regret trying to use me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–157<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Flashback to the first semester&#x27;s closing ceremonies: Chabashira calls him to the faculty room the moment homeroom ends, before summer vacation can start.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I don’t remember doing anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Why did you sound all sarcastic?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Where do you think? I got called over by the teacher, so I don’t really have a choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening banter turns on Sudou after he is named as the first speaker; the lines are recorded by turn.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t say such nonsense—”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gets his wrists grabbed in both meaty hands for a wingman request there is no time to accept.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reaches the faculty room to find Chabashira waiting in the doorway.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t understand why you called me over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what did you want to talk to me about? I’m busy planning my summer vacation right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I was exaggerating when I said that. I have at least a few friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before that, should we have tea? You must be thirsty,”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Checks the kitchenette is empty first — the talk is to happen where there are no eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another abstract question, I see. Is it okay if I say I think you’re beautiful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm… Well, if you don’t mind being compared to other teachers, I … think you don’t care at all about Class D’s future, and that you’re a cold … teacher with no interest in her students. That’s my answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gives her the unsoftened verdict against Hoshinomiya and Sakagami, and reads her bloodlust under the joke without taking it back.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I must say that’s surprising. I would’ve thought you were more capable, Chabashira-sensei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m guessing someone made a trivial mistake, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not catching your drift. What does this have to do with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What am I supposed to say to that? You’re joking, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He said to expel me? Well, that’s nonsense. I don’t know who it was, but you ignored his request and won’t have me expelled. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I don’t intend to do anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you threatening me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I go now? I won’t listen to any more of this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Reaches over the desk and grabs her collar to quote her own lesson back at her — the discomfort she made Horikita feel, shoes in someone&#x27;s home.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll probably regret trying to use me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His answer is never spoken on the page; the warning reads as acceptance, but the scene closes on her line instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"ch 5  5 2  the faculty room deal closing ceremonies  she catches him the moment homeroom ends   faculty room  before he leaves   and gives nothing else away until the door shuts   ayanokouji  i have to talk to you before you leave  come to the faculty room   come in   we ll talk inside   you might expect bad things when you re asked to come to the faculty room  but contrary to your expectations  it s a fine place  there aren t eyes all around in here  many things are better said with some personal privacy   that s funny  i thought you didn t have any friends   i ve called you here today because i wanted to tell you my personal story   it s something i haven t talked to anyone about since i had become a homeroom teacher  it s silly  but please listen   don t tell this story to anyone else  if you can do that  please return to your seat   how do i appear to you as class d s homeroom teacher   am i wrong   no  it s as you say  i won t deny it  however  the truth is different   i was once a student at this school  i was in class d  just like you   huh  well  in my time  the class difference wasn t as extreme  you could say that we were in a four way battle  not a three way one  up until we approached graduation in the third semester of our third year  the difference between a and d wasn t even 100 points  it was a close battle  where even one trivial mistake could knock you off balance   yes  it happened rather unexpectedly  class c went to hell because of my mistake  in the end ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p152-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–157<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closing ceremonies: she catches him the moment homeroom ends — faculty room, before he leaves — and gives nothing else away until the door shuts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Ayanokouji. I have to talk to you before you leave. Come to the faculty room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Come in.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “We’ll talk inside.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>31 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waits in the faculty-room doorway and answers in short sentences that raise his “incoming depression” meter.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might expect bad things when you’re asked to come to the faculty room, but contrary to your expectations, it’s a fine place. There aren’t eyes all around in here. Many things are better said with some personal privacy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Uses a faculty room whose security camera is missing — privacy is the point of the venue.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s funny. I thought you didn’t have any friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve called you here today because I wanted to tell you my personal story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s something I haven’t talked to anyone about since I had become a homeroom teacher. It’s silly, but please listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t tell this story to anyone else. If you can do that, please return to your seat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How do I appear to you as Class D’s homeroom teacher?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, it’s as you say. I won’t deny it. However, the truth is different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Owns the cold-teacher verdict outright, then opens with the reason behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was once a student at this school. I was in Class D, just like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> She sat where he sits — a student of this school, in Class D, once.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh… Well, in my time, the class difference wasn’t as extreme. You could say that we were in a four-way battle, not a three-way one. Up until we approached graduation in the third semester of our third year, the difference between A and D wasn’t even 100 points. It was a close battle, where even one trivial mistake could knock you off balance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Her era at the school: four classes fighting as four, A and D under 100 points apart until the third semester of the third year — set against the three-way school he knows.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. It happened rather unexpectedly. Class C went to hell because of my mistake. In the end, my goal of reaching Class A and my dreams were shattered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> One trivial mistake sent Class C down and ended her Class A dream — the regret the narration reads as still live.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I feel that your presence will be vital to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A few days ago, a certain man contacted the school directly. He said ‘expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. We can’t just expel someone on a third party’s whim. As long as you are a student at this school, you are protected by the rules. However…if you cause any problems, that’s a different story. Smoking, bullying, stealing, cheating… If you cause any scandal, expulsion is unavoidable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It has nothing to do with your intentions. If I determine that something seems like an issue, it will become reality.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The rule she wields: protection stands until she decides something is a problem — then the scandal, not the intent, decides the expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Here’s the deal, Ayanokouji. You are going to aim for Class A for me. I will follow up as extensively as I can in order to protect you. Don’t you think that sounds like a good offer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Names it a deal and dresses the pressure as protection — the narration calls it blackmailing a student outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s too bad, Ayanokouji. You will be expelled, and once again, Class D won’t reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me ask you once more. Will you aim for Class A? Or be expelled? You choose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes the collar grab over the desk, then laughs in self-deprecation — the confidence breaks and the old dream shows.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I surprised myself. I realize now that I still haven’t given up on reaching Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d thought you would lead Class D voluntarily, but we don’t have any time to waste. You have to decide here and now. Will you help me or not?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Relax. My life is already full of regrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> By the end the cold indifference is gone — misty-eyed and forceful, the act put away.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.8: she announces the retirement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 2  the invitation at her desk closing ceremonies at her desk neighbour s side  sudou s summer invitation arrives the moment the bell rings   why   how stupid  it doesn t matter at all that it s summer vacation  why are you even inviting me out in the first place","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–153<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closing ceremonies at her desk neighbour’s side; Sudou’s summer invitation arrives the moment the bell rings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “How stupid. It doesn’t matter at all that it’s summer vacation. Why are you even inviting me out in the first place?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Refuses him flatly, then finishes getting ready and leaves the classroom without another word while he is still mid-pitch.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The call that opens the exchange and the sign-off at the end are untagged between the three of them; both are left with the chapter’s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"ch 5  5 2  the invitation that fails closing ceremonies  the moment the bell rings he goes after horikita with a summer invitation   why  did you do something   yeah  you re not good or bad  you live a plain  boring  steady life   sarcastic  i didn t mean to  did it feel like it   hey  horikita  um  well  since it s summer vacation are you free  maybe we can hang out a little   well  because it s summer vacation  you know  it d be too bad if you didn t have fun  we can watch movies or go shopping   wh why  why are you being so obtuse   well  it s just like that  you know  right  guys invite girls out when it s a holiday   hey  where are you going   can you wait just a little  just a bit   you re gonna watch me do battle  be my wingman   damn  guess it was useless after all  well  guess i ll go do club stuff","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p152-1\">Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation that fails<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–153<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closing ceremonies: the moment the bell rings he goes after Horikita with a summer invitation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Why? Did you do something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Yeah. You’re not good or bad. You live a plain, boring, steady life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Sarcastic? I didn’t mean to. Did it feel like it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The banter before the invitation turns untagged after he is named as the first speaker; the lines are recorded by turn.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Horikita. Um, well, since it’s summer vacation…are you free? Maybe we can hang out a little.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The vacation invite — movies or shopping — meets a flat refusal; she sees no reason for the invitation at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, because it’s summer vacation, you know? It’d be too bad if you didn’t have fun. We can watch movies or go shopping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “‘Wh-why’? Why are you being so obtuse?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it’s just like that, you know? Right? Guys invite girls out when it’s a holiday…”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey! Where are you going?”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you wait just a little? Just a bit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re gonna watch me do battle. Be my wingman.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs Ayanokōji’s wrists in both meaty hands and will not let go until he promises to watch the battle.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recruits him as wingman for a pitch that loses its audience when Chabashira’s call pulls him away.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn. Guess it was useless after all. Well, guess I’ll go do club stuff.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Watches Horikita leave without a glance back — dumbfounded — and falls back on club practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1–§2.5: the toilet, the leader card, and a first calm intervention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
